hearing over the law had an awkward tone, one day after the Justice Department changed its position on a key issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CORPUS CHRISTI, Tex. — For several days in 2014 at the federal courthouse here, lawyers argued over whether the Texas Legislature had passed its voter identification law motivated, at least in part, by a desire to deter minorities from voting. Lawyers for the Justice Department said it had, as did lawyers for minority voters and civil rights groups. Lawyers for Texas denied the allegation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Was Texas Voter ID Law Biased? Justice Dept. Stays Out of Argument', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justice Department Stays Out of Argument Over Intent of Texas Voter ID Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramos, Nelva Gonzales', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paxton, Ken', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gupta, Vanita', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-01T02:06:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez and Eric Lichtblau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1},