ect', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "National People's Congress (China)", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-02T17:09:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sui-Lee Wee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sui-lee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3119c38a-538f-5c26-a73c-3cfa89a4f177', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3119c38a-538f-5c26-a73c-3cfa89a4f177'}, {'abstract': 'The designer may not be as serious as his clothes would suggest, but he’s every bit as brilliant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/02/t-magazine/rick-owens-fashion-designer.html', 'snippet': 'The designer may not be as serious as his clothes would suggest, but he’s every bit as brilliant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YOU KIND OF WANT the fashion designer Rick Owens to be a monosyllabic, misanthropic recluse. It’s what the embodiment of his clothes should be, if we were going by some unwritten aesthetic script. After all, the fashion Owens presents four times a year, for men and women, on the grand Paris stage, isn’t free and easy. It isn’t simple. It often looks like rags: Precious fabrics, like cashmere, are pilled and laddered, and leather is repeatedly washed to give it the texture and appearance of a prehistoric animal’s skin. There is something monstrous about his gothic garments, with their strange, disturbing proportions attenuated and exaggerated, draped like ectoplasm clinging to thin limbs. When people wear them head