f882e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/66939466-027c-534a-acf6-bcc6228f882e'}, {'abstract': 'In this drama directed by Udi Aloni, Tamer Nafar plays an Arab Israeli citizen trying to build a music career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/02/movies/junction-48-review.html', 'snippet': 'In this drama directed by Udi Aloni, Tamer Nafar plays an Arab Israeli citizen trying to build a music career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Familiar genre trappings do little to dispel the groove of “Junction 48,” which does for the Israeli city of Lod what “8 Mile” aimed to do for the suburbs of Detroit. This energetic drama from the Israeli-American director Udi Aloni casts the real-life rapper Tamer Nafar as Kareem, an aspiring musician from the mixed-population city (also Mr. Nafar’s hometown), where Kareem, one of Israel’s Arab citizens, faces regular discrimination and the feeling of a dead end.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/03/arts/03JUNCTION/03JUNCTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 296, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/03/arts/03JUNCTION/03JUNCTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 296}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/03/arts/03JUNCTION/03JUNCTION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 505, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/03/arts/03JUNCTION/03JUNCTION-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 1627, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/03/arts/03JUNCTION/03JUNCTION-thumbSta