s', '_id': 'nyt://article/816a71f0-d608-562d-84f4-c1e8f4faa3a3', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/816a71f0-d608-562d-84f4-c1e8f4faa3a3'}, {'abstract': 'A snap election on March 2 created a virtual tie between the Catholic nationalist party and its main Protestant rival, the Democratic Unionists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/04/world/europe/northern-ireland-election-sinn-fein.html', 'snippet': 'A snap election on March 2 created a virtual tie between the Catholic nationalist party and its main Protestant rival, the Democratic Unionists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBLIN — Sinn Fein, the main Catholic nationalist party in Northern Ireland, has won its greatest share of legislative seats ever after a snap election, creating a virtual tie with its Protestant rivals and throwing nearly two decades of peaceful power sharing into turmoil.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Northern Ireland Voters Give Sinn Fein Its Biggest Win Ever', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Political Pivot in Northern Ireland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northern Ireland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sinn Fein', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Unionist Party (Northern Ireland)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-04T19:23:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': "By Sinead O'Shea", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sinead', 'middlename