ssociates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalio, Raymond (1949- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-06T01:35:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8368337-7601-5e64-8bcd-690d2d4340c8', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8368337-7601-5e64-8bcd-690d2d4340c8'}, {'abstract': 'It’s not every firm where a top executive is accused of lying on a video for every employee to see. But that’s how Ray Dalio runs Bridgewater Associates, according to former employees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/05/business/dealbook/ex-employees-note-a-hint-of-turmoil-in-bridgewaters-recipe-for-success.html', 'snippet': 'It’s not every firm where a top executive is accused of lying on a video for every employee to see. But that’s how Ray Dalio runs Bridgewater Associates, according to former employees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is not every workplace where a top executive is accused of lying on a video for every employee to see. It is also unusual for a company founder to fire an employee in a group email and then later dismiss it as simply a joke.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/06/business/06DB-HEDGE/06DB-HEDGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/06/business/06DB-HEDGE/06DB-HEDGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/06/business/06DB-HEDGE/06DB-HEDGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height