The brand has no presence on social media, and their first lookbook — which stars the half-Chilean and half-English indie actor Cosme Castro — includes unglamorous behind-the-scenes images rather than anything posed or polished. And despite an accomplished résumé that, between them, includes stints at Adam Kimmel, Alexander Wang and A.P.C, the “about” section of Cobra’s website is just an embedded YouTube playlist featuring the Stone Roses and Raekwon. “It felt most natural to explain ourselves through our influences instead of with words,” Taghizadeh said. “We’re not into this idea that you’re pushing an idea more than a product,” added Reynolds.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brand to Know: The Men’s Wear Line Rethinking the Button-Down Shirt', 'kicker': 'On the Verge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Stuffed Shirts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-06T19:44:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Hawgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hawgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/943c0d74-c416-5298-b881-f17432422f75', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/943c0d74-c416-5298-b881-f17432422f75'}, {'abstract': '“Cursed Child” earned 11 nominations, including best new play; “Groundhog Day” received eight nominations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/06/theater/harry-potter-and-the-cursed-child-ties-record-for-most-olivier-nominations.html', 'snippet': '“Cursed Child” earned 11 nominations, including best new play; “Groundhog Day” received eight nominations.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Harry Potter and the Cursed Child” received 11 Olivier nominations on Monday, tying “Hairspray” for the most in the awards’ history. J. K. Rowling’s latest addition to the Harry Potter canon will compete for best new play and several acting and design awards before its scheduled transfer to Broadway next year. It was conceived by Ms. Rowling with its playwright, Jack Thorne, and director, John Tiffany.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/07/arts/07olivier-item/07olivier-item-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/07/arts/07olivier-item/07olivier-item-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/07/arts/07olivier-item/07olivier-item-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/07/arts/07olivier-item/07olivier-item-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/07/arts/07olivier-item/07olivier-item-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/07/arts/07olivier-item/07olivier-item-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/07/arts/07olivier-item/07