'Judge Platt also presided over suits against Libya and Pan American World Airways in the terrorist bombing of a jet over Lockerbie, Scotland, in 1988.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thomas C. Platt, a federal judge in New York who warned the nation’s air traffic controllers in 1981 about severe penalties if they went on an illegal strike, and then fined their union $100,000 an hour when they did, prompting President Ronald Reagan to fire them, died on Saturday in North Branford, Conn. He was 91.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/07/sports/07platt-obit/07platt-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/07/sports/07platt-obit/07platt-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/07/sports/07platt-obit/07platt-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/07/sports/07platt-obit/07platt-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/07/sports/07platt-obit/07platt-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/07/sports/07platt-obit/07platt-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/07/sports/07platt-obit/07platt-obit-thumb