url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/07/movies/kong-skull-island-and-other-kong-movies.html', 'snippet': 'Since his debut in 1933, King Kong keeps getting rebooted. Here’s a look at what all those remakes mean, including the latest, “Kong: Skull Island.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since the first “King Kong” movie in 1933, the giant, chest-pounding, helicopter-smacking, no-nonsense primate has meant different things to different generations, embodying both his science and his fiction. Kong has been a kind of canvas on which to paint the economic and political issues of the time. He’s hovering larger than ever (along with a starry cast) in “Kong: Skull Island” (in theaters March 10). Here is a look back at versions of Kong and the themes that went with the roars.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/07/arts/kong-compare-top/kong-compare-top-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/07/arts/kong-compare-top/kong-compare-top-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/07/arts/kong-compare-top/kong-compare-top-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/07/arts/kong-compare-top/kong-compare-top-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 857, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/07/arts/kong-compare-top/kong-compare-top-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail'