 ‘Scared They’ll Take Away Our Children’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Certificates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-08T10:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deborah Acosta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deborah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Acosta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d780b26-9157-57d7-ac5e-d34cff756a20', 'word_count': 1036, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d780b26-9157-57d7-ac5e-d34cff756a20'}, {'abstract': 'Our rising dependence on cameras is changing our language, and the company behind Snapchat is counting on the eventual dominance of visual culture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/08/technology/snap-makes-a-bet-on-the-cultural-supremacy-of-the-camera.html', 'snippet': 'Our rising dependence on cameras is changing our language, and the company behind Snapchat is counting on the eventual dominance of visual culture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re watching Snap’s stock ticker, stop. The company that makes Snapchat, the popular photo-messaging app, has been having a volatile few days after its rocket-fueled initial public offering last week.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/09/technology/09state-illo/09state-illo-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'lega