/article/40efa74e-f49f-5cea-8f7f-945c5d82f8b6', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40efa74e-f49f-5cea-8f7f-945c5d82f8b6'}, {'abstract': 'Also, a middle-aged son who refuses to dress up, wayward email and the neighbor you know too well.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/09/fashion/social-qs-news-detox-boyfriend.html', 'snippet': 'Also, a middle-aged son who refuses to dress up, wayward email and the neighbor you know too well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lately I’ve been feeling depressed about the news, so I decided to avoid it. I shared my decision with my boyfriend, and he seemed to understand. But just as I was feeling better, he reported an awful headline that was devastating to me. I confronted him about how his behavior affected me, and he gave me a weak “Sorry.” Now he acts as if all is normal. But all is not normal. I feel terrible again, and I think I deserve a proper apology. How should I express this?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type