ition, at Luhring Augustine, is a kind of poignant self-portrait of Mr. Wolfe, who died last year and whose art centered on meticulous sculptures of books.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/09/arts/design/steve-wolfe-remembering-steve-speaks-volumes-about-an-artist.html', 'snippet': 'This exhibition, at Luhring Augustine, is a kind of poignant self-portrait of Mr. Wolfe, who died last year and whose art centered on meticulous sculptures of books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steve Wolfe, an artist who died last year at 60, was known for the small, select library of trompe l’oeil books he created. From his first solo show in 1989, Wolfe’s sculptures and wall pieces were all-but-perfect replicas of worn, well-used copies of modern classics and artist monographs and catalogs — usually his own — tweaked to within a hair of the original. Initially anonymous and ordinary in appearance, these copies become exquisitely personal as you grasp the level of skill and commitment required to make them. They are labors of love.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/arts/10WOLFE1/10WOLFE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/10/arts/10WOLFE1/10WOLFE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/arts/10WOLFE1/10WOLFE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/arts/10WOLFE1/10WOLFE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1539, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/arts/10WOLFE1/10WOLFE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/10/arts/10WOLFE1/10WOLFE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/arts/10WOLFE1/10WOLFE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Steve Wolfe: Remembering Steve’ Speaks Volumes About an Artist', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolfe, Steve (1955-2016)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Luhring Augustine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-09T23:23:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5a40c27-9b1e-5b69-8bdc-2b304cb73f71', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5a40c27-9b1e-5b69-8bdc-2b304cb73f71'}, {'abstract': 'The third season of this ABC anthology series offers a central story line about farmworkers in North Carolina. The drama is unblinking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/09/arts/television/review-american-crime-season-3-abc.html', 'snippet': 'The third season of this ABC anthology series offers a central story line about farmworkers in North Carolina. The drama i