hy is California still officially in a drought? We answer some questions Californians, and others, may have.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The Hollywood Reservoir is nestled in a basin surrounded, usually, by dusty brown hillsides, broken up by the occasional dry wisp of shrubbery. Not these days. After yet another burst of rain the other day, the hills were transformed into lush fields of knee-high grass, spotted with purple flowers. And the reservoir? As high as it has been in years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/us/00-Drought-sub/00-Drought-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/10/us/00-Drought-sub/00-Drought-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/us/00-Drought-sub/00-Drought-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/us/00-Drought-sub/00-Drought-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/10/us/00-Drought-sub/00-Drought-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/us/00-Drought-sub/00-Drought-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/us/00-Drought-sub/00-Drought-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Is a Drought Over? A Wet California Wants to Know', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Water Rises, but California Bides Its Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-10T10:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb7f1fe2-2f33-5e9a-ad04-817634210bcb', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb7f1fe2-2f33-5e9a-ad04-817634210bcb'}, {'abstract': 'A good mother does bad things on behalf of her bullied son. Should she feel triumphant or ashamed?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/10/style/modern-love-when-a-mom-bullies-back.html', 'snippet': 'A good mother does bad things on behalf of her bullied son. Should she feel triumphant or ashamed?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many years ago, I threw a playground ball at the head of a boy who was repeatedly dunking my young son underwater. Before I threw the ball, I shouted at him to stop, but he continued. I was at the other end of the pool, maybe a six-second swim away, but my 5-year-old son was gasping and pleading, and the fastest way to make my point was to throw the ball.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None,