ocument_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Viet Thanh Nguyen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Viet', 'middlename': 'Thanh', 'lastname': 'Nguyen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cd2521d-8263-5f74-9341-32c7dbb0372e', 'word_count': 1227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cd2521d-8263-5f74-9341-32c7dbb0372e'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Loizzo likes to cook and socialize with her neighbors in the Mott Haven section of the Bronx. That includes a potluck dinner with family and friends every other week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/10/nyregion/gigi-loizzo-guggenheim-museum-sunday-routine.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Loizzo likes to cook and socialize with her neighbors in the Mott Haven section of the Bronx. That includes a potluck dinner with family and friends every other week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the director of retail strategy and operations for the Guggenheim Museum, Gigi Loizzo selects the items sold in the museum’s store and is in charge of building its e-commerce site. She commutes into Manhattan from her home in the Mott Haven section of the Bronx five days a week, so on the weekends, she prefers to keep things local. Ms. Loizzo, 55, lives in a townhouse with her husband, Angel Molina, 57, a recent retiree; their daughter, Maya Luz Molina, 29, an accessories designer; their three dogs, Bruno, Bad Betty and Larry; and a cat, New Kitty.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1/12ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/12/nyregion/12ROUTINE1/12ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xla