': 'nyt://article/2300e06f-1765-5f2a-a6d7-f0dba5f43241'}, {'abstract': 'The show features work from the late 1930s and early 1940s by one of the 20th century’s most important American painters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/10/arts/design/true-north-marsden-hartleys-maine-at-the-met-breuer.html', 'snippet': 'The show features work from the late 1930s and early 1940s by one of the 20th century’s most important American painters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The painter Marsden Hartley (1877-1943) ranged far and wide during his career, but when he returned to his home state for good in 1937, declaring his intention to be “the painter of Maine,” he seemed to find an intellectual birthright he had been seeking his whole life.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/12/arts/12GUIDE3/12GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/12/arts/12GUIDE3/12GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/12/arts/12GUIDE3/12GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/12/arts/12GUIDE3/12GUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1342, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/12/arts/12GUIDE3/12GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/12/arts/12GUIDE3/12GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailw