azz musician from Norway hunted bits of cosmic debris for eight years and found it everywhere. Turns out, tons of it land every day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/10/science/space-dust-on-earth.html', 'snippet': 'A jazz musician from Norway hunted bits of cosmic debris for eight years and found it everywhere. Turns out, tons of it land every day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After decades of failures and misunderstandings, scientists have solved a cosmic riddle — what happens to the tons of dust particles that hit the Earth every day but seldom if ever get discovered in the places that humans know best, like buildings and parking lots, sidewalks and park benches.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/11/science/14SCI-STARDUST-COMP01/14SCI-STARDUST-COMP01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/11/science/14SCI-STARDUST-COMP01/14SCI-STARDUST-COMP01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 613}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/11/science/14SCI-STARDUST-COMP01/14SCI-STARDUST-COMP01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1002, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/11/science/14SCI-STARDUST-COMP01/14SCI-STARDUST-COMP01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2004, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/11/science/14SCI-STARDUST-COMP01/14SCI-STARDUST-COMP01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'