rganization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71ceac00-bb83-573b-b83c-3af604f4cdbe', 'word_count': 690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71ceac00-bb83-573b-b83c-3af604f4cdbe'}, {'abstract': 'A fashion show that resembled performance art, Nicki Minaj’s surprise look — and a Chanel rocket. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/10/t-magazine/fashion/top-10-moments-paris-fashion-week-nicki-minaj-chanel-rocket.html', 'snippet': 'A fashion show that resembled performance art, Nicki Minaj’s surprise look — and a Chanel rocket. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paris Fashion Week marked a few important milestones: The designer Dries Van Noten held his 100th runway show, a celebratory marker of a brilliant career. The collection, which featured vibrant prints, oversize silhouettes and jewel-toned faux fur jackets, was modeled by the greatest names in the business, including Amber Valletta, Nadja Auermann and Kirsten Owen — all models who have walked in Van Noten’s shows since 1993. Later in the week, Jean Touitou of A.P.C. celebrated his 30th year in business with an intimate show at the brand’s studio on the Left Bank. The collection was about simplicity, but done well: there were no-fuss denim jackets, pants, trench coats and military dresses. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/t-magazine/fashion/top-ten-paris-slide-ZUD0/top-ten-paris-slide-ZUD0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/10/t-magazine/fashion/top-ten-paris-slide-ZUD0/top-ten-paris-slide-ZUD0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/t-magazine/fashion/top-ten-paris-slide-ZUD0/top-ten-paris-slide-ZUD0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683