States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-11T00:58:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4364cf88-f132-5e46-8809-c9c87056abaf', 'word_count': 1210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4364cf88-f132-5e46-8809-c9c87056abaf'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer has a fascination with Midtown Manhattan: “It’s kind of a time capsule of New York."', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/10/style/daniel-arnold-the-look.html', 'snippet': 'The photographer has a fascination with Midtown Manhattan: “It’s kind of a time capsule of New York."', 'lead_paragraph': 'Daniel Arnold has a fascination with Midtown Manhattan — “It’s kind of a time capsule of New York,” he said — and that’s where most of these photos were taken, between November and January. A photographer with over 135,000 followers on Instagram, Mr. Arnold is known for finding humor in everyday New York moments, like people standing around eating hot dogs or dogs pulling on their walkers. In this case, he was also looking for the lively and eccentric style found on the city’s wintry streets. He walked us through the moments he captured below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daniel Arnold’s Tongue-in-Cheek Take on New York Style', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords'