d caused the “largest humanitarian crisis in the world.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANA, Yemen — An airstrike by a military coalition led by Saudi Arabia on an open market in western Yemen killed at least 16 people, United Nations and local officials said Saturday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yemen Market Airstrike Kills at Least 16 People', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yemen Airstrike Kills at Least 16', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Brien, Stephen Rothwell (1957- )", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-11T14:32:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shuaib Almosawa and Ben Hubbard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shuaib', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Almosawa', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hubbard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67ee248f-2fab-57ac-a17f-69447addc232', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67ee248f-2fab-57ac-a17f-69447addc232'}, {'abstract': 'Boards are protected by the business judgment rule, which gives them wide legal latitude in the decisions they make.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/11/realestate/is-a-co-op-required-to-report-break-ins-to-shareholders.html', 'snippet': 'Boards are protected by the business judgment rule, which gives them wide legal latitude in the decisions they make.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. In January, a burglar slipped into our  co-op in Hudson Heights, Manhattan, behind a shareholder who was walking out. He stole a laundry cart  and  packages. The theft was reported to the police, but it took the board almost two weeks to notify shareholders. The notice minimized the event, failing to give a full account of it. What responsibility does the board have to shareholders  in reporting security breaches?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/12/realestate/12ASK/12ASK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 109, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/12/realestate/12ASK/12ASK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 109}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/12/realestate/12ASK/12ASK-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 186, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/12/realestate/12ASK/12ASK-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/12/realestate/12ASK/12ASK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/12/realestate/12ASK/12ASK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/12/realestate/12ASK/12ASK-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is a Co-op Required to Report Break-Ins to Sharehold