': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0bfd1ed-f93a-522d-a6bb-f7461171c5ee', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0bfd1ed-f93a-522d-a6bb-f7461171c5ee'}, {'abstract': 'The pastry chef Rory Macdonald’s new Pâtisserie Chanson serves breakfast pastries and light lunches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/13/dining/patisserie-chanson-pastry-chef-rory-macdonald.html', 'snippet': 'The pastry chef Rory Macdonald’s new Pâtisserie Chanson serves breakfast pastries and light lunches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rory Macdonald’s Pâtisserie Chanson opens March 20. The pastry shop and bread bakery is a highly ambitious debut for the chef. In addition to a typical ground-floor retail counter, with communal seating and an open kitchen, the bakery includes a subterranean dessert bar for sweet tasting menus, to open soon. Mr. Macdonald, a London native whose baking is decidedly French, was the pastry chef for Hakkasan restaurants in America. He makes eight kinds of bread, breakfast pastries, fancy cakes, individual pastries and chocolates. Soups, salads, sandwiches and a proper afternoon tea will be served in the ground-floor dining area: Pâtisserie Chanson, 20 West 23rd Street, 929-423-8880, patisseriechanson.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15BURNER-BAKERY/15BURNER-BAKERY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15BURNER-BAKERY/15BURNER-BAKERY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15BURNER-BAKERY/15BURNER-BAKERY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15BURNER-BAKERY/15BURNER-BAKERY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15BURNER-BAKERY/15BURNER-BAKERY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15BURNER-BAKERY/15BURNER-BAKERY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15BURNER-BAKERY/15BURNER-BAKERY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Croissants for the Flatiron District', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Visit: More Croissants and Cakes for the Flatiron District', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Patisserie Chanson (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Macdonald, Rory (Chef)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pastries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Flatiron District (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-13T17:35:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37629acd-e50c-5bda-9b45-51bba34f91a5', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37629acd-e50c-5bda-9b45-51bba34f91a5'}, {'abstract': 'At Orchard Grocer on the Lower East Side, carrots are treated like smoked fish and jackfruit is drenched in barbecue sauce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/13/dining/vegan-orchard-grocer-lower-east-side.html', 'snippet': 'At Orchard Grocer on the Lower East Side, carrots are treated like smoked fish and jackfruit is drenched in barbecue sauce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No, that is not smoked salmon in the deli case of the new vegan Orchard Grocer. It is smoked carrots effectively presented in salmon garb — sliced thin, the color of sockeye, and well cured in the kinds of pickling spices used for the fish. “I want to be playful and witty,” said Joya Carlton, the executive chef and an alumna of Butcher’s Daughter and Buvette. Ms. Carlton shows her Virginia roots with “pulled” jackfruit, shredded in barbecue sauce on a bun. Orchard Grocer is owned by the sisters Sara and Erica Kubersky, who also own MooShoes next door, and carries nut-milk cheeses, condiments, chocolates and other foods. “This whole world of vegan has exploded,” Ms. Carlton said: Orchard Grocer, 78 Orchard Street (Broome Street), 646-757-9910, orchardgrocer.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15BURNER-GROCERY/15BURNER-GROCERY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15BURNER-GROCERY/15BURNER-GROCERY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15BURNER-GROCERY/15BURNER-GROCERY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name