view-african-art-in-a-game-of-catch-up.html', 'snippet': 'Small galleries are spotlighting the work of Mor Faye, Ernest Mancoba and others from the continent, although big museums have shown little interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York is catching up on Africa’s modern art history, though our big museums aren’t much in the picture. Two of that continent’s leading 20th-century painters are having first major solos here, not at the Museum of Modern Art or the Guggenheim, but at small downtown galleries. And a remarkable contemporary artist collective from the Democratic Republic of Congo is making its New York debut at an alternative space in Queens.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/14/arts/14AFRICANART2/14AFRICANART2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/14/arts/14AFRICANART2/14AFRICANART2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 755}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/14/arts/14AFRICANART2/14AFRICANART2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 814, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/14/arts/14AFRICANART2/14AFRICANART2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1628, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/14/arts/14AFRICANART2/14AFRICANART2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/14/arts/14AFRICANART2/14AFRICANART2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailh