tweeted about a Lawfare post — without realizing it was highly critical of him — he sent its readership skyrocketing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A little over a year ago, Benjamin Wittes, the editor in chief of the blog Lawfare, made the case that Donald Trump, as a Republican presidential candidate, represented nothing less than a national-security threat. “Never before in my lifetime has either political party been led by a man with such an unusual combination of — from a national security perspective, anyway — terrifying liabilities,” Wittes wrote. Ticking off reasons ranging from his promise of a Muslim ban to his flirtation with Vladimir Putin, Wittes stressed Trump’s propensity for promising outcomes through force of personality rather than policies and programs. “In the national security space, it is a particularly pernicious lie,” he concluded. “Our tools are too dangerous.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/14/magazine/14mag-lawfare/14mag-lawfare-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/14/magazine/14mag-lawfare/14mag-lawfare-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/14/magazine/14mag-lawfare/14mag-lawfare-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/14/magazine/14mag-lawfare/14mag-lawfare-jumbo.png', 'height': 274, 'width': 597, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/14/magazine/14mag-lawfare/14mag-lawfare-superJumbo.png', 'height': 274, 'width': 597, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How a Wonky National-Security Blog Hit the Big Time', 'kicker': 'Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brookings Institution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-14T09:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Bazelon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bazelon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b8084e0-6fdb-5f06-9b9a-506b6dd96f89', 'word_count': 1479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b8084e0-6fdb-5f06-9b9a-506b6dd96f89'}, {'abstract': 'Is the bracket competition more fun than the actual game? Why or why not?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/14/learning/what-do-you-enjoy-about-using-brackets-for-sports-competitions.html', 'snippet': 'Is the bracket competition more fun than the actual game? Why or why not?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Will you be filling out a bracket for the N.C.A.A. men’s basketball tournament this year? Will you be watching the games?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/10/sports/wackybracket-illo/wackybracket-illo-thumbStandard-v2.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/10/sports/wackybracket-illo/wackybracket-illo-t