': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosalie R. Radomsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosalie', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Radomsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04a50036-e384-5f39-8f24-01044cfbbb01', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04a50036-e384-5f39-8f24-01044cfbbb01'}, {'abstract': 'Real populism doesn’t sell, but fake populism has problems too.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/03/14/populism-and-the-politics-of-health/', 'snippet': 'Real populism doesn’t sell, but fake populism has problems too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s next on health care? Truly, I have no idea. The AHCA is a real stinker, and now everyone knows it; ordinarily, that should doom the legislation. But everyone also knows that starting off the Trump legislative era with the crashing and burning of Obamacare repeal would deeply damage Trump; nobody believes what he says, but if he can’t even ram bills through, people will stop being afraid. So they will pull out all the stops.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Populism and the Politics of Health', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-03-14T17:43:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5abf453c-5b54-528e-b929-7647b4e2a6c5', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5abf453c-5b54-528e-b929-7647b4e2a6c5'}, {'abstract': 'The Velvet Underground and Nico performed in downtown Manhattan before recording a debut LP; the show was captured by Larry Morris.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/14/arts/music/velvet-underground-lou-reed-nico-photos.html', 'snippet': 'The Velvet Underground and Nico performed in downtown Manhattan before recording a debut LP; the show was captured by Larry Morris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A half a century ago this month, the Velvet Underground released its debut LP, “The Velvet Underground & Nico.” That enduringly transgressive album would go on to earn the music-industry axiom, first voiced by Brian Eno, that although relatively few people bought it initially, everyone who did started a band.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/14/arts/music/15VELVETS-slide-AJAX/15VELVETS-slide-AJAX-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/14/arts/music/15VELVETS-slide-AJAX/15VELVETS-slide-AJAX-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/14/arts/music/15VELVETS-slide-AJAX/15VELVETS-slide-AJAX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/14/arts/music/15VELVETS-slide-AJAX/15VELVETS-slide-AJAX-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/14/arts/music/15VELVETS-slide-AJAX/15VELVETS-slide-AJAX-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'t