'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Price, Thomas E (1954- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-14T20:29:13+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By DAVE HORN, DAPHNE RUSTOW, MEG FELLING and MARK SCHEFFLER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'HORN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Daphne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'RUSTOW', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Meg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'FELLING', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SCHEFFLER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/975cc563-8283-5079-a234-6af630489176', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/975cc563-8283-5079-a234-6af630489176'}, {'abstract': 'The 2017 festival at City Center has been dominated by women — and has a standout in Patricia Guerrero.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/14/arts/dance/flamenco-fest-its-a-womans-womans-womans-world.html', 'snippet': 'The 2017 festival at City Center has been dominated by women — and has a standout in Patricia Guerrero.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Patriarchal codes may still have force in Spanish society, but contemporary flamenco is seldom a man’s world. Flamenco Festival 2017, like many Flamenco Festivals past, has been dominated by women. In the two shows at City Center last week, only one had an overtly feminist theme: Olga Pericet’s “Pisadas.” The other, “Gala Flamenca,” was just a gala — one that happened to be ruled by women.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/arts/15FLAMENCOROUNDUP-WEB1/15FLAMENCOROUNDUP-WEB1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/15/arts/15FLAMENCOROUNDUP-WEB1/15FLAMENCOROUNDUP-WEB1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/arts/15FLAMENCOROUNDUP-WEB1/15FLAMENCOROUNDUP-WEB1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/arts/15FLAMENCOROUNDUP-WEB1/15FLAMENCOROUNDUP-WEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/15/arts/15FLAMENCOROUNDUP-WEB1/15FLAMENCOROUNDUP-WEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/arts/15FLAMENCOROUNDUP-WEB1/15FLAMENCOROUNDUP-WEB1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/arts/15FLAMENCOROUNDUP-WEB1/15FLAMENCOROUNDUP-WEB1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Flamenco Fest: It’s a Woman’s Woman’s Woman’s World', 'kicker': "Critic's Notebook", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s a Woman’s Woman’s Woman’s World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flamenco (Dance)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pericet, Olga', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carmona, Jesus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guerrero, Patricia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-14T20:40:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c96f6f52-bb95-5dba-9c28-dfeb7cb277bb', 'word_count': 793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c96f6f52-bb95-5dba-9c28-dfeb7cb277bb'}, {'abstract': 'Jean-Pierre Frohlich of the New York City Ballet talks about teaching “The Cage,” a stylized Jerome Robbins work, to the Bolshoi dancers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/14/arts/dance/interview-bolshoi-ballet-staging-jerome-robbins-the-cage.html', 'snippet': 'Jean-Pierre Frohlich of the New York City Ballet talks about teaching “The Cage,” a stylized Jerome Robbins work, to the Bolshoi dancers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1951, “The Cage” shocked the world. Prickly and intense, this Jerome Robbins ballet concerns a female-dominated world where acts of violence are everyday occurrences. A Novice is born into an insect tribe, led by a Queen. Instinctively, the Novice knows what to do when a male intruder enters: She crushes his neck between her knees. She falls in love with a second intruder, but in the end, kills him, too. Her backup is a 12-strong corps de ballet whose killer instincts and hair — so teased that it stands on end — give the ballet a spooky, feral pulse.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/arts/15THECAGE2/15THECAGE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/15/arts/15THECAGE2/15THECAGE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/arts/15THECAGE2/15THECAGE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/arts/15THECAGE2/15THECAGE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/15/arts/15THECAGE2/15THECAGE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/arts/15THECAGE2/15THECAGE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/arts/15THECAGE2/15THECAGE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Look Pretty! Staging a Feral Robbins Ballet at the Bolshoi', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Have Strength. And Don’t Look Pretty!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Cage (Ballet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bolshoi Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frohlich, Jean-Pierre', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbins, Jerome', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-14T20:42:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a89e890-8f69-59f4-b3a8-5f1c6d6b4b14', 'word_count': 859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a89e890-8f69-59f4-b3a8-5f1c6d6b4b14'}, {'abstract': 'A financial district offering from the team behind Blue Ribbon; Jonathan Benno to leave Lincoln Ristorante; Le Périgord closes; and other restaurant news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/14/dining/majorelle-lowell-hotel-jonathan-benno.html', 'snippet': 'A financial district offering from the team behind Blue Ribbon; Jonathan Benno to leave Lincoln Ristorante; Le Périgord closes; and other restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MAJORELLE The new restaurant in the Lowell Hotel is finally about to open. Taking a look at the elegant dining room designed by Michael S. Smith, and its château-worthy architectural details like engaged columns and egg-and-dart moldings, it’s easy to understand why it took so long. Past a leather-trimmed bar called Jacques (as in the artist Jacques Majorelle, whose gardens are a treasure of Marrakesh, Morocco), the restaurant has 75 or so seats, about 20 of them in a compact, skylit garden, and a comfortable library/lounge with a fireplace is adjacent to the dining room. Charles Masson, one of the city’s rare guardians of classic French cuisine and service, will run the restaurant. And, with Christian Delouvrier consulting and Mr. Masson’s input, the chef, Mario Fortuna, is creating a menu he described as marrying traditional French with the Mediterranean, even crossing the sea for an occasional taste of Morocco, with a tagine. Highlights include a rich onion tart, warm sausage with potatoes, risotto of wild mushrooms, bass with Champagne and caviar, and steak au poivre. There will be tableside service for carving a chicken for two and finishing a baba au rhum. The pastry chef, David Carmichael, will produce breads from grains milled in-house. “You can’t beat fresh flour for nutrition,” he said. A bar menu has lighter fare like chicken liver mousse and ceviche, but it’s not above offering a hamburger. (Opens Wednesday): 28 East 63rd Street, 212-935-2888, majorelleny.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/dining/15OFF/15OFF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Majorelle, Offering French Fare in the Lowell Hotel, to Open', 'kicker': 'Off the Menu', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Financial District (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Majorelle (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Masson, Charles Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-14T20:54:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c216c0d4-fcc2-5fbc-86dd-fff0c8531af3', 'word_count': 1359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c216c0d4-fcc2-5fbc-86dd-fff0c8531af3'}, {'abstract': 'Check out the theater, dance and museum deals we found for snow-drenched tourists and families with cabin fever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/14/arts/ticket-discounts-cancellations-broadway.html', 'snippet': 'Check out the theater, dance and museum deals we found for snow-dren