Jonah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fd2f5c5-2bc8-5fb4-bd18-78f432990d29', 'word_count': 4708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fd2f5c5-2bc8-5fb4-bd18-78f432990d29'}, {'abstract': 'The Ethicist columnist on suspecting a possibly factitious disorder and whether to call out someone’s racist joke.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/15/magazine/should-a-family-member-expose-their-nieces-fake-food-allergy.html', 'snippet': 'The Ethicist columnist on suspecting a possibly factitious disorder and whether to call out someone’s racist joke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My brother and I suspect that our sister-in-law has either embellished the extent of our niece’s food allergy or made it up completely. The same holds true for the child’s “asthma.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/magazine/19ethicist/19ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/19/magazine/19ethicist/19ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/magazine/19ethicist/19ethicist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/magazine/19ethicist/19ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 964, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/19/magazine/19ethicist/19ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 964}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/magazine/19ethicist/19ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 638, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/magazine/19ethicist/19ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1076, 'width': 670, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Should a Family Member Expose a Niece’s Fake Food Allergy?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'May I Expose My Niece’s Fake Food Allergy?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALLERGIES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-15T09:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc3bc157-2eaf-5312-b0a8-a23e4b30efb2', 'word_count': 1148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc3bc157-2eaf-5312-b0a8-a23e4b30efb2'}, {'abstract': 'The congressional candidate on what the Republican Party is doing right and how being a Gamergate target prepared her to run for office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/15/magazine/brianna-wu-wants-to-change-the-democrats-playbook.html', 'snippet': 'The congressional candidate on what the Republican Party is doing right and how being a Gamergate target prepared her to run for office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many people are familiar with you as a prime target of Gamergate, a harassment campaign against women in the video-game community. Considering the flood of abuse you received, why would you decide to do something as high-profile as run for Congress? It’s terrifying, right? The thing Gamergate taught me is that there’s nothing I can’t handle. What is someone going to do: Call me ugly? Threaten to kill me? I already deal with all of that on a daily basis. I realized I needed to do this in a business meeting after election night, where I couldn’t even concentrate because I was so upset. I knew I wouldn’t feel good about just making video games for the next four years.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '58', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/magazine/19talk/19mag-19talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/19/magazine/19talk/19mag-19talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/magazine/19talk/19mag-19talk-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 438, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/magazine/19talk/19mag-19talk-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 876, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/magazine/19talk/19mag-19talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/19/magazine/19talk/19mag-19talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75