terial': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5deb00da-5fdb-5cbc-92be-4260835a6121', 'word_count': 1028, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5deb00da-5fdb-5cbc-92be-4260835a6121'}, {'abstract': 'I trusted USA Gymnastics, but its institutional tolerance of abusive training helped create a culture conducive to sexual abuse.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/03/15/cracking-down-on-abuse-in-u-s-gymnastics/', 'snippet': 'I trusted USA Gymnastics, but its institutional tolerance of abusive training helped create a culture conducive to sexual abuse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The day I found my sport, rhythmic gymnastics, was the day I fell in love with it. Those first few years of training were pure bliss, but to achieve my goal of becoming a world-class athlete, I needed to switch to an elite coach. My first practice with my new coach was so intense that I spent the following two days vomiting and unable to make it back to practice. When I did return, the work began. By age 15, I was U.S. national champion, a position I held for three years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/13/opinion/13kristof_blog/13kristof_blog-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 539, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/13/opinion/13kristof_blog/13kristof_blog-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 539}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/13/opinion/13kristof_blog/13kristof_blog-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 862, 'width': 960, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/13/opinion/13kristof_blog/13kristof_blog-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 862, 'width': 960, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, '