g Ms. Hamill as Marianne Dashwood, a fun-loving romantic with a reckless heart.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE7/19GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE7/19GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE7/19GUIDE7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE7/19GUIDE7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE7/19GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE7/19GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE7/19GUIDE7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Vanity Fair’ at the Pearl Theater Brings William Makepeace Thackeray to the Stage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Theater; Social Climbing and Clawing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pearl Theater Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thackeray, William Makepeace', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamill, Kate A (1981- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tucker, Eric (Theater Director)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Vanity Fair (Play)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-15T15:47:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Collins-Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins-Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c6423e8-a49a-555f-8d50-432f16b9f387', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c6423e8-a49a-555f-8d50-432f16b9f387'}, {'abstract': 'In addition to Mr. Morris’s modern work, the lineup includes Richard Alston’s “Sheer Bravado” and Nacho Duato’s “Por Vos Muero.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/15/arts/dance/juilliard-dances-repertory-brings-mark-morriss-v-back-to-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'In addition to Mr. Morris’s modern work, the lineup includes Richard Alston’s “Sheer Bravado” and Nacho Duato’s “Por Vos Muero.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Juilliard bustles come spring — not only are seniors auditioning like mad, but students of all levels also gear up for Juilliard Dances Repertory, an annual showcase of works by established choreographers. This year’s lineup, which begins Wednesday, March 22, features Richard Alston’s “Sheer Bravado” (2006), a dance for 10 originally set to Shostakovich, and Nacho Duato’s “Por Vos Muero” (1996), a heady work that uses the Spanish guitar music and poetry of Garcilaso de la Vega. But the high point is Mark Morris’s “V” (2001), an enduring modern dance set to Robert Schumann’s Quintet in E flat Major for Piano and Strings, Op. 44. “V” could reference the number five — there is the quintet itself — or the birdlike shapes the dancers make with their arms as they soar across the stage. It could be the victory sign. But Sept. 11, 2001, was on many minds when the work debuted in New York. Mr. Morris, in fact, dedicated it to the city. What else could “V” be? Peace. (Through March 25, Peter Jay Sharp Theater; events.juilliard.edu.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE6/19GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE6/19GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE6/19GUIDE6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE6/19GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE6/19GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE6/19GUIDE6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE6/19GUIDE6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1387, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Juilliard Dances Repertory Brings Mark Morris’s ‘V’ Back to New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance; ‘V’ Is a Shape of Many Meanings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alston, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duato, Nacho', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-15T15:48:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d26b7f1b-8496-5a6b-b432-64a7407f174b', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d26b7f1b-8496-5a6b-b432-64a7407f174b'}, {'abstract': '“The Brit New Wave” program will offer 30 films, including Paul Richardson’s “A Taste of Honey” and “The Loneliness of the Long Distance Runner.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/15/movies/everything-british-including-the-kitchen-sink-at-film-forum.html', 'snippet': '“The Brit New Wave” program will offer 30 films, including Paul Richardson’s “A Taste of Honey” and “The Loneliness of the Long Distance Runner.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The soot and the soul are palpable in “The Brit New Wave,” a 30-film program at Film Forum from Wednesday, March 22, through April 6. It celebrates British cinema of the late 1950s and ’60s, not least the era’s kitchen-sink dramas. Such movies introduced the likes of the directors Karel Reisz, John Schlesinger and Tony Richardson, whose unflinching focus on the urban working class, depicted with a dignity and honesty, has fresh relevance amid contemporary America’s economic chasm. Friday has the singular “A Taste of Honey” (1961), from Shelagh Delaney’s pungent 1958 play. Jo (Rita Tushingham, a 19-year-old newcomer then) is encumbered by her slattern mother (Dora Bryan). When Jo’s romance with a sailor results in pregnancy, a gay textile designer (Murray Melvin) helps out. Shot by the cinematographer Walter Lassally, often in the smokestack-laden precincts of Greater Manchester, “Honey” could inspire 1,000 album covers for the Smiths. It runs with Richardson’s “The Loneliness of the Long Distance Runner” (1962). (filmforum.org)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE3/19GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE3/19GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE3/19GUIDE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE3/19GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 623, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE3/19GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 623}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE3/19GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 739, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/arts/19GUIDE3/19GUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 739, 'subTyp