': 'The internet has been a great destroyer of cultural businesses. Its toll includes getting people accustomed to listening to music and consuming news without paying, and it has freed people to cut the cable cord.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tech Roundup: The Internet’s Creative Side Takes Off', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-15T16:56:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pui-Wing Tam', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pui-wing', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tam', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c80333fd-1815-5b0a-b6a4-ce37beb9ac8d', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c80333fd-1815-5b0a-b6a4-ce37beb9ac8d'}, {'abstract': 'To help teachers make the most of these films, we also provide a grab-bag of teaching ideas, related readings and student activities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/15/learning/lesson-plans/25-mini-films-for-exploring-race-bias-and-identity-with-students.html', 'snippet': 'To help teachers make the most of these films, we also provide a grab-bag of teaching ideas, related readings and student activities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How do we get students to consider perspectives different from their own? How do we get them to challenge their own biases and prejudices? If, as Atticus Finch famously said, “You never really understand a person until you consider things from his point of view … until you climb into his skin and walk around in it,” how do we get our students to do that?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '26 Mini-Films for Exploring Race, Bias and Identity With Students', 'kicker': 'Film Club', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-03-15T17:09:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'subsection_name': 'Lesson Plans', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1242cf76-16b1-5717-b569-a74e944cd9d7', 'word_count': 1302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1242cf76-16b1-5717-b569-a74e944cd9d7'}, {'abstract': 'Both rulings — the one in Hawaii more expansive than the one in Maryland — said the likely purpose of the president’s order was a de facto ban on Muslims.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/15/us/politics/trump-travel-ban.html', 'snippet': 'Both rulings — the one in Hawaii more expansive than the one in Maryland — said the likely purpose of the president’s order was a de facto ban on Muslims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge in Hawaii issued a nationwide order Wednesday evening blocking President Trump’s ban on travel from parts of the Muslim world, dealing a stinging blow to the White House and signaling that Mr. Trump will have to account in court for his heated rhetoric about Islam.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 Federal Judges Rule Against Trump’s Latest Travel Ban', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Federal Judge  Blocks New Ban on Travel to U.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chuang, Theodore D', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watson, Derrick Kahala', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-15T17:22:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7c00b63-f31e-5eb0-af4e-002c8a75773d', 'word_count': 1808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7c00b63-f31e-5eb0-af4e-002c8a75773d'}, {'abstract': 'After Brian C. Vigneault died near the end of a 24-hour live stream, many players acknowledged the health risks of a culture that rewards those who stay online for hours.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/15/technology/personaltech/live-streaming-gaming-death.html', 'snippet': 'After Brian C. Vigneault died near the end of a 24-hour live stream, many players acknowledged the health risks of a culture that rewards those who stay online for hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early on Feb. 19, Brian C. Vigneault was nearing the end of a 24-hour marathon of live streaming himself playing the tank warfare video game World of Tanks when he left his computer to buy a pack of cigarettes. He never returned.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'im