 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/16/world/16IRAN4/16IRAN4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/16/world/16IRAN4/16IRAN4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/16/world/16IRAN4/16IRAN4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/16/world/16IRAN4/16IRAN4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fireworks Offer an Illicit Thrill Ahead of Iranian New Year', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'vis-dispatch', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tehran (Iran)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fireworks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-15T17:35:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/919fd183-bf41-56f6-8c76-71bf51fe757a', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/919fd183-bf41-56f6-8c76-71bf51fe757a'}, {'abstract': 'In a majestic 19th-century space in Paris, Joseph Dirand let his imagination run wild, without parameters (not even livability).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/15/t-magazine/design/joseph-dirand-designer-paris-apartment-avenue-montaigne.html', 'snippet': 'In a majestic 19th-century space in Paris, Joseph Dirand let his imagination run wild, without parameters (not even livability).', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNTIL RECENTLY, the Parisian designer and architect Joseph Dirand savored the boundaries built into his profession; he was certain that limits focused him, or at least that there was value in the elaborate dance of convincing clients to do things his way. Still, even at his rarefied level, there were practical concerns as well as budgets, albeit often stupendous ones. At its Surf Club residences in Miami, whose rooms Dirand swathed in travertine, the Four Seasons handed him a 700-page book of guidelines; the Balenciaga showroom in Toyko — that showcased the dreamy, uninterrupted expanses of rare marble that the 43-year-old Dirand so loves — had a mission to sell merchandise and the L’Apogée Courchevel resort had to be finished ahead of time for the resort’s brief ski season.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '178', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/t-magazine/dirand-slide-C6FJ-copy/dirand-slide-C6FJ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 430, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/15/t-magazine/dirand-slide-C6FJ-copy/dirand-slide-C6FJ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 430}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/15/t-magazine/dirand-slide-C6FJ-copy/dirand-slide-C6FJ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jum