ubject', 'value': 'Blindness', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Macular Degeneration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clinical Trials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'US Stem Cell Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institutes of Health', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Journal of Medicine', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-15T21:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denise Grady', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grady', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/381724f2-ddab-5c4c-9ad3-68ae713b36ac', 'word_count': 1411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/381724f2-ddab-5c4c-9ad3-68ae713b36ac'}, {'abstract': 'The Fed seems to believe it has reached a sweet spot after nearly eight years of trying to nurse the economy back to health.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/15/upshot/yellens-message-my-work-here-is-mostly-done.html', 'snippet': 'The Fed seems to believe it has reached a sweet spot after nearly eight years of trying to nurse the economy back to health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The economy will keep growing just enough to put more Americans back to work, but without overheating to generate excessive inflation. American workers will see gradual pay raises that keep compensation rising faster than inflation. Interest rates will rise gradually, while staying low by historical standards. And that’s all before accounting for any major stimulative policies that may emerge from the Trump administration and Congress.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/16/upshot/16up-fed/16up-fed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/16/upshot/16up-fed/16up-fed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/16/upshot/16up-fed/16up-fed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/16/upshot/16up-fed/16up-fed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/16/upshot/16up-fed/16up-fed-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/16/upshot/16up-fed/16up-fed-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/16/upshot/16up-fed/16up-fed-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yellen’s Message: My Work Here Is (Mostly) Done', 'kicker': 'Monetary Policy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Fed’s Message: Exhale', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yellen, Janet L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-15T21:01:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Irwin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Irwin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2b017d4-0689-5a3f-a758-bdcf8f961580', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2b017d4-0689-5a3f-a758-bdcf8f961580'}, {'abstract': 'You’ll need some luck to win, but this table can help by looking at differences between experts and the wisdom of crowds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/15/upshot/a-contrarian-cheat-sheet-improve-your-ncaa-bracket.html', 'snippet': 'You’ll need some luck to win, but this table can help by looking at differences between experts and the wisdom of crowds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whoever wins an N.C.A.A. tournament bracket has to have some luck. That goes for small office pools as well as big national contests. It’s essentially impossible to pick a perfect bracket, which is why Warren Buffett once offered $1 billion to anyone who did.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Contrarian Cheat Sheet: Improve Your N.C.A.A. Bracket', 'kicker': 'Everyone in the Pool', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCA