nded and necessary corrective to the growth of the government’s power. But even members of his own party questioned some of the cuts — and what was not being cut.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/us/17budget1/17budget1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/17/us/17budget1/17budget1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/us/17budget1/17budget1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/us/17budget1/17budget1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/17/us/17budget1/17budget1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/us/17budget1/17budget1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/us/17budget1/17budget1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1279, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Takes a Gamble in Cutting Programs His Base Relies On', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump Gambles in Cutting Services That Aid His Base', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-16T19:07:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/423d484f-d42e-51ec-ada5-8b65b4e8c211', 'word_count': 1274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/423d484f-d42e-51ec-ada5-8b65b4e8c211'}, {'abstract': 'The fashion designer and the artist sat down with T to discuss their creative processes — and current exhibitions. (Anderson’s curatorial debut opens this weekend.)', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/16/t-magazine/jonathan-anderson-anthea-hamilton-conversation-art-fashion.html', 'snippet': 'The fashion designer and the artist sat down with T to discuss their creative processes — and current exhibitions. (Anderson’s curatorial debut opens this weekend.)', 'lead_paragraph': '“This is the most unbelievably comfortable seat,” says the Irish fashion designer Jonathan Anderson as he nestles into a Modernist Danish chair at the Hepworth Wakefield gallery in Yorkshire, in the north of England. “I could just sit here forever,” agrees the Turner-nominated artist Anthea Hamilton softly, as she settles in alongside Anderson. They are immersed in Hamilton’s exhibition there, where she explores early British Modernist works from the Kettle’s Yard house — an art gallery and onetime home of the influential late collector Jim Ede in Cambridge, England. (Hamilton curated pieces from the space, which is currently closed and being remodeled, for the installation, which also includes contemporary works). Her show has a certain stillness — a stark contrast to the gallery rooms next door, where the finishing touches of Jonathan Anderson’s curatorial debut, “Disobedient Bodies,” are being put precisely into place.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/16/t-magazine/16tmag-jw-anthea-slide-B3S2/16tmag-jw-anthea-slide-B3S2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 481, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/16/t-magazine/16tmag-jw-anthea-slide-B3S2/16tmag-jw-anthea-slide-B3S2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 481}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/16/t-magazine/16tmag-jw-anthea-slide-B3S2/16tmag-jw-anthea-slide-B3S2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 821, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/16/t-magazine/16tmag-jw-anthea-slide-B3S2/16tmag-jw-anthea-slide-B3S2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1642, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/16/t-magazine/16tmag-jw-anthea-slide-B3S2/16tmag-jw-anthea-slide-B3S2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/16/t-magazine/16tmag-jw-anthea-slide-B3S2/16tmag-jw-anthea-slide-B3S2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/16/t-magazine/16tmag-jw-anthea-slide-B3S2/16tmag-jw-anthea-slide-B3S2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 