are the team for No. 1 Villanova?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/16/sports/ncaabasketball/mount-st-marys-villanova.html', 'snippet': 'Mount St. Mary’s played one of the country’s top nonconference schedules this season. But did it prepare the team for No. 1 Villanova?', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUFFALO — Miles Wilson’s first college game was on the road in front of more than 10,000 fans in Morgantown, W.Va., where the West Virginia Mountaineers beat his Mount St. Mary’s Mountaineers by nearly 30. Eight more road games followed, a trip, designed partly to raise the program’s visibility, that left Mount St. Mary’s with a 1-8 record but also the experience of playing two major-conference champions and six total teams that ended up in the N.C.A.A. tournament.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/sports/17MOUNTSTMARYS/17MOUNTSTMARYS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/17/sports/17MOUNTSTMARYS/17MOUNTSTMARYS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/sports/17MOUNTSTMARYS/17MOUNTSTMARYS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/sports/17MOUNTSTMARYS/17MOUNTSTMARYS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 826, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/17/sports/17MOUNTSTMARYS/17MOUNTSTMARYS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 826}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/sports/17MOUNTSTMARYS/17MOUNTSTMARYS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 744, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/sports/17MOUNTSTMARYS/17MOUNTSTMARYS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1488, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tested Early, and Again by Draw, Mount St. Mary’s Says It’s Ready', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Mount St Mary's University (Emmitsburg, Md)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NCAA Basketball Championships (Men)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-16T21:15:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Tracy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tracy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95aa50a2-f566-589b-a423-b350ac1c0378', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95aa50a2-f566-589b-a423-b350ac1c0378'}, {'abstract': 'A statue intended as a symbol of women’s power may be Instagram-friendly, but it’s a covert exercise in corporate imaging, our columnist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/16/nyregion/fearless-girl-statue-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'A statue intended as a symbol of women’s power may be Instagram-friendly, but it’s a covert exercise in corporate imaging, our columnist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the moment that “Fearless Girl,” a bronze statue of a small child, landed in Lower Manhattan to face off against the 7,000-pound sculpture of a charging bull, installed in 1989 as a symbol of Wall Street resilience, there were reasons, it seemed, to feel queasy. Where, for instance, was her nanny? While others saw a narrative of female defiance — the girl’s torso thrusts forward as if she has a chance — I imagined a poorly paid caregiver fired for leaving her charge unattended, and ultimately trampled to death.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/nyregion/19BIG1/19BIG1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 383, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/19/nyregion/19BIG1/19BIG1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 383}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/nyregion/19BIG1/19BIG1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/nyregion/19BIG1/19BIG1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1277, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/nyregion/19BIG1/19BIG1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/19/nyregion/19BIG1/19BIG1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/nyregion/19BIG1/19BIG1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The False Feminism of ‘Fearless Girl’', 'kicker': 'Big City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Fearless Girl’ and False Feminism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deferred Prosecution Agreements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Street Global Advisors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Street Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Letitia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-16T21:19:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a955ea9f-edd3-5674-9657-61252bd808be', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a955ea9f-edd3-5674-9657-61252bd808be'}, {'abstract': 'Our guide to stand-up, improv and variety shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/16/arts/comedy-in-nyc-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Our guide to stand-up, improv and variety shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our guide to stand-up, improv and variety shows.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/arts/17LISTINGSCOMEDY/17LISTINGSCOMEDY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/17/arts/17LISTINGSCOMEDY/1