5a78-bd2c-af834fcb8962'}, {'abstract': 'Alexei Ratmansky’s “Whipped Cream,” performed by American Ballet Theater, turns frothy nonsense into inspired enchantment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/16/arts/dance/review-alexei-ratmansky-whipped-cream-american-ballet-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Alexei Ratmansky’s “Whipped Cream,” performed by American Ballet Theater, turns frothy nonsense into inspired enchantment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COSTA MESA, Calif. — The virtues of “Whipped Cream,” American Ballet Theater’s new two-act creation, are many and important — though it’s bizarre to speak of “importance” in a piece about a sweetshop coming to life. Alexei Ratmansky, resident artist with the troupe since 2009, is the choreographer: The world premiere occurred on Wednesday here at the Segerstrom Center for the Arts. The score is Richard Strauss’s “Schlagobers” (1924) — surely until now the most generally forgotten ballet music by a major composer.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/arts/17RATMANSKYSUB1/17RATMANSKYSUB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 364, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/17/arts/17RATMANSKYSUB1/17RATMANSKYSUB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 364}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/arts/17RATMANSKYSUB1/17RATMANSKYSUB1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 621, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/arts/17RATMANSKYSUB1/17RATMANSKYSUB1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1213, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None