': 735, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65a5f80b-0598-5d43-8537-553e2608cb10'}, {'abstract': 'A New York Times photographer went to the Korean city that will host the 2018 Winter Olympics and attended events offering a taste of what is to come.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/17/sports/olympics-pyeongchang-winter-games-2018.html', 'snippet': 'A New York Times photographer went to the Korean city that will host the 2018 Winter Olympics and attended events offering a taste of what is to come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pyeongchang will host Korea’s first Winter Olympics in February. The New York Times photographer Chang W. Lee, who left South Korea 30 years ago, returned last month to visit the region where the 2018 Games will be held. The trip brought back memories of the seven Olympics he has covered for The Times — which gave him a front-row seat for the struggles, the beauty, the smiles and the tears that make the Olympics one of his favorite events. But the trip also brought a sense of anticipation, a sense that a new set of magic moments, a new wave of drama, was on its way again, and this time in Korea, his home.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/sports/19OLYMPICS2/19PYEONGCHANGweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/19/sports/19OLYMPICS2/19PYEONGCHANGweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/sports/19OLYMPICS2/19PYEONGCHANGweb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/sports