 Jürgen Flimm has returned to the Metropolitan Opera to brush up his 2000 production. Our lead critic says his participation pays off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How does an opera company keep an ambitious production vibrant and vital when it’s revived? The best way, of course, is to bring back the original director, something Peter Gelb, the Met’s general manager, has tried over the years. Because these artists are often busy elsewhere, revivals are routinely entrusted to an in-house stage director, who basically recreates the original while taking some liberties and adapting the concept to new casts.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/18/arts/18FIDELIO/18FIDELIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/18/arts/18FIDELIO/18FIDELIO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/18/arts/18FIDELIO/18FIDELIO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/18/arts/18FIDELIO/18FIDELIO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1358, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/18/arts/18FIDELIO/18FIDELIO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/18/arts/18FIDELIO/18FIDELIO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u