 Huget leaves no letter behind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY PUZZLE — I do try to pick fun pictures for the top of this blog, people. I try to follow the rules, be relevant and not too loopy, but today I stumbled on this awesome little metaphor for modern times, the glofish™. Thanks to years of high-end scientific research, the embryo of a perfectly fine little zebra fish (among other species) is injected with a single gene to produce fluorescence; for its entire life, then, and for our entertainment, this little fish is like a neon beacon flittering nervously through its watery environment, uncamouflaged unless it gets lucky enough to wind up in a submerged ‘80s nightclub.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/18/crosswords/18wordplay-zebrafish/18wordplay-zebrafish-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/18/crosswords/18wordplay-zebrafish/18wordplay-zebrafish-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/18/crosswords/18wordplay-zebrafish/18wordplay-zebrafish-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/18/crosswords/18wordplay-zebrafish/18wordplay-zebrafish-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1182, 'width': 1677, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/18/crosswords/18wordplay-zebrafish/18wordplay-zebrafish-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/18/crosswords/18wordplay-zebrafish/18wordplay-zebrafish-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/18/crosswords/18wordplay-zebrafish/18wordplay-zebrafish-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Think Over', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Think Over', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-18T02:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fb8cac0-9e0f-51dd-8073-d08398e08a17', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fb8cac0-9e0f-51dd-8073-d08398e08a17'}, {'abstract': 'President Trump has managed to anger British officials with his claims about spying.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/17/opinion/london-ridicules-the-ridiculous.html', 'snippet': 'President Trump has managed to anger British officials with his claims about spying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Will President Trump ever learn — or care — that his fact-free tweets have painful consequences, not just at home but abroad? Surely he must sense this by now, as the administration faces the outrage of British allies who have been dragged into his increasingly bogus allegation that he was spied on by the Obama administration.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'