Great Barrier Reef will signal the decline of the ocean environment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/18/opinion/shed-a-tear-for-the-reefs.html', 'snippet': 'Until global warming is fully addressed, places like the Great Barrier Reef will signal the decline of the ocean environment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reports that the Great Barrier Reef is dying come ever more frequently, ever more urgently. There is no mystery about the reason — it’s global warming, caused by the fossil fuels we burn. If we stopped heating the oceans, parts of the great reef off Australia’s north coast and other spectacular coral reefs around the world could still recover. The alternative is to weep at the loss of one of the most spectacular sights on earth, as the author of the latest report and his students did on examining charts of the damage.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/opinion/sunday/19sun2/19sun2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/19/opinion/sunday/19sun2/19sun2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 723}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/opinion/sunday/19sun2/19sun2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 851, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/opinion/sunday/19sun2/19sun2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1166, 'width': 968, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/opinion/sunday/19sun2/19sun2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/19/opinion/sunday/19sun2/19sun2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/opinion/sunday/19sun2/19sun2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shed a Tear for the Reefs', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shed a Tear for the Reefs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Barrier Reef (Australia)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature (Journal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'El Nino Southern Oscillation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reefs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coral', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-18T21:07:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/db0b43e3-f8e1-5389-950b-5f4c1415be36', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db0b43e3-f8e1-5389-950b-5f4c1415be36'}, {'abstract': 'It wouldn’t be prudent to hold a plebiscite before the Brexit process concludes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/18/opinion/sunday/scottish-independence-can-wait.html', 'snippet': 'It wouldn’t be prudent to hold a plebiscite before the Brexit process concludes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British were fully warned before they voted to quit the European Union that this also risked a breakup of the United Kingdom. When a majority of Scots voted against breaking with Britain in 2014, they were not then voting to break with the European Union, and their preference for staying in the union was firmly confirmed when 62 percent voted against Brexit in the referendum in June 2016. So the call by Nicola Sturgeon, head of the Scottish National Party and first minister of Scotland, for another Scottish referendum on independence should come as no surprise to Westminster.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/opinion/19sun3web/19sun3web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/19/opinion/19sun3web/19sun3web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/opinion/19sun3web/19sun3web-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/opinion/19sun3web/19sun3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/19/opinion/19sun3web/19sun3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/opinion/19sun3web/19sun3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':