'}, {'abstract': 'Grant Thackray makes his debut as “that guy.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/18/crosswords/111-across.html', 'snippet': 'Grant Thackray makes his debut as “that guy.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY PUZZLE — If you think about it, one of evolution’s driving factors is the element of surprise — either how to win at it and be a successful predator, or how to detect it and avoid being lunch. So just as our primal brain is wired to relish solving puzzles as an extension of more dire problems of survival, we must have a deep connection to the notion of the cliffhanger. There are probably phenotypes who relish suspense, and those who just can’t look when things get too tense (that’d be me), and, oh yes, those people who must ruin it for everyone else by peeking, figuring it out or seeing it first, then providing loud, enthusiastic, advance narration, to put it kindly. I suppose it’s not a purely malevolent urge; after all, I’d have totally appreciated it if, in my past life as a Neanderthal, I was told that the saber-toothed tigers had recently moved to a cave on my polished-rock delivery route, and therefore I could work from home that day. I would really have appreciated that!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/crosswords/19wordplay-canal/19wordplay-canal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/19/crosswords/19wordplay-canal/19wordplay-canal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/crosswords/19wordplay-canal/19wordplay-canal-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': No