Dies at 88', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breslin, Jimmy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-19T13:59:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/33b32864-07f1-578e-8960-a9863d776d5a', 'word_count': 2496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33b32864-07f1-578e-8960-a9863d776d5a'}, {'abstract': 'The 37-acre Woodland Cemetery, which dates to Newark’s 19th-century heyday, has become a haven for crime and a scene of disrepair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/19/nyregion/a-historic-new-jersey-cemetery-sits-neglected-and-blighted.html', 'snippet': 'The 37-acre Woodland Cemetery, which dates to Newark’s 19th-century heyday, has become a haven for crime and a scene of disrepair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK — Every Mother’s Day, Ann Jeffress and her two sisters have come to Woodland Cemetery here to lay a rose at the grave of their mother, Lucy. The visits were never easy, but now they have become traumatic in ways they never imagined. When the women enter the cemetery, they walk hand in hand, clutching sticks to fend off dogs or potential attackers. They poke cautiously through mounds of rubble in search of the spot where their mother was laid to rest.', 'print_section': 'A', 'pri