on': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/6f712d70-bec4-5698-9078-53f97ea4db0c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/6f712d70-bec4-5698-9078-53f97ea4db0c'}, {'abstract': 'An online fight against posting of women’s nude photos by male groups of Marines and veterans has been fortified by criticism of the practice by Jim Mattis, a cult figure in the corps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/19/insider/marine-nude-photo-scandal-jim-mattis.html', 'snippet': 'An online fight against posting of women’s nude photos by male groups of Marines and veterans has been fortified by criticism of the practice by Jim Mattis, a cult figure in the corps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent weeks, a widening scandal has erupted over secret all-male groups of Marines and veterans that posted nude photos of female Marines online without their knowledge and consent, and often included names, ranks and where the women were stationed. A new article, the third I’ve done on the unfolding scandal, reports on young Marine veterans who have taken up the fight against the harassment online, saying the Marine Corps leadership is not sure how to tackle the problem. But as is often true, there are interesting side stories that don’t make it into the main report. Such is the case with the inspiration for some of the anti-harrassment efforts: Saint Mattis.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/18/insider/18A2ITT/18A2ITT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/18/insider/18A2ITT/18A2ITT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/18/insider/18A2ITT/18A2ITT-t