f striving newcomers (Holly Macve).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/19/arts/music/sxsw-south-by-southwest-best-music.html', 'snippet': 'This year’s festival featured reunions (At the Drive-In), memorials (for Buckwheat Zydeco) and a range of striving newcomers (Holly Macve).', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUSTIN, Tex. — All sorts of metrics are applied to digital-era music to measure success: sales, streams, radio plays, tickets. One that’s harder to measure, and therefore often ignored, is audience joy. That’s where the South by Southwest Music Festival comes in. With audiences in which badge-holding music-business professionals are surrounded by more typical listeners, the festival provides instant feedback on what’s really reaching people: via shouts, singalongs, rowdy approval or rapt attention. At a time when the music business and the tech companies that now dominate it are concentrating on a customized experience, SXSW shows how much people still prize a communal one.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/arts/20SXSW-DAMEBLANCE/20SXSW-DAMEBLANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/20/arts/20SXSW-DAMEBLANCE/20SXSW-DAMEBLANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/arts/20SXSW-DAMEBLANCE/20SXSW-DAMEBLANCE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/arts/20SXSW-DAMEBLANCE/20SXSW-DAMEBLANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/20/arts/20SXSW-DAMEBLANCE/20SXSW-DAMEBLANCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/arts/20SXSW-DAMEBLANCE/20SXSW-DAMEBLANCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/arts/20SXSW-DAMEBLANCE/20SXSW-DAMEBLANCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding the Joy at South by Southwest: 12 Notable Acts', 'kicker': "Critic's Notebook", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding Festival Joy, Communally', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'South by Southwest Music and Media Conference', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Garth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Residente (Rapper)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-19T22:20:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c836d37a-0036-532f-a70a-f731156ef227', 'word_count': 1441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c836d37a-0036-532f-a70a-f731156ef227'}, {'abstract': 'Works by Mr. Perich, combining gritty one-bit electronic sounds with live music, were performed at the Kitchen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/19/arts/music/review-tristan-perich-the-kitchen.html', 'snippet': 'Works by Mr. Perich, combining gritty one-bit electronic sounds with live music, were performed at the Kitchen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While many composers working with electronic resources these days tout the sophistication of their experiments, Tristan Perich does almost the opposite. For years he has worked with a technology he unabashedly describes as lo-fi, gritty, one-bit sound. Mr. Perich’s pieces and sound-art installations use one-bit electronics, which, if I understand it (and I’m not sure I do), involves electronic music that never has more than one bit of information at any given moment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/arts/20PERICH/20PERICH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/20/arts/20PERICH/20PERICH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/arts/20PERICH/20PERICH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/arts/20PERICH/20PERICH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/20/arts/20PERICH/20PERICH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/arts/20PERICH/20PERICH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/arts/20PERICH/20PERICH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJ