ion/billions-currency-recap.html', 'snippet': 'Chuck eats a sandwich; Wags meets an old mentor; both have plenty to chew on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sunday night’s episode of “Billions” is book ended, improbably, by Johnny Cash’s cover of “(I’d Be) a Legend in My Time,” a country song that Don Gibson wrote and recorded in 1960 and Cash recorded shortly before he died, as part of his “American” collaboration with producer Rick Rubin. (The cover appears on “American V: A Hundred Highways.”) It seems peculiar to lay a stripped-down, mournful country track over Wags’s peeling into Axe Capital or Chuck’s tearing through a sandwich after a major arrest. But when you consider the last three lines, the theme of the episode emerges:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/watching/19billions/19billions-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/19/watching/19billions/19billions-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/watching/19billions/19billions-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/watching/19billions/19billions-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/19/watching/19billions/19billions-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/watching/19billions/19billions-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_