nippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Sunday, March 19, 2017.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because of an editing lapse, a review on March 5 about Megan Marshall’s biography “Elizabeth Bishop: A Miracle for Breakfast” neglected to note that the reviewer, Langdon Hammer, is working on his own critical biography of Bishop.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Editors’ Note: March 19, 2017', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2017-03-20T04:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/d00835ce-6973-50f9-a031-3960e2cd516c', 'word_count': 37, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d00835ce-6973-50f9-a031-3960e2cd516c'}, {'abstract': 'Ceferin, “the candidate of change,” figures it is time to shake up, yet still protect, the soccer in Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/20/sports/soccer/uefa-aleksander-ceferin.html', 'snippet': 'Ceferin, “the candidate of change,” figures it is time to shake up, yet still protect, the soccer in Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NYON, Switzerland — When Aleksander Ceferin talks about changes, he means the grand, sweeping variety. He means the sort that might begin to repair the “stained” reputation of football’s governing bodies: things like term limits and transparency, the policies that helped elect him president of UEFA by a landslide in September.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/sports/20ONSOCCERweb1/20ONSOCCERweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy':