, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4525bd2-e40d-5cec-b12c-375f34880824', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4525bd2-e40d-5cec-b12c-375f34880824'}, {'abstract': 'The Nazis pressed Henryk Ross into service as the official photographer in the Lodz ghetto in Poland, where he also surreptitiously recorded the devastating realities of daily life.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/03/20/a-jewish-photographers-view-of-a-nazi-controlled-ghetto-henryk-ross/', 'snippet': 'The Nazis pressed Henryk Ross into service as the official photographer in the Lodz ghetto in Poland, where he also surreptitiously recorded the devastating realities of daily life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In March 1945 a man who had witnessed far too much human misery dug into ground hardened by the Polish winter and retrieved what he had buried months earlier. Thus, in a manner of speaking, did he provide the dead with an afterlife.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Jewish Photographer Documented a Nazi-Controlled Ghetto', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concentration Camps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ross, Henryk', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ART GALLERY OF ONTARIO', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of Fine Arts (Boston)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lodz (Poland)', 'rank': 11, 'm