— The Provisional Government this morning issued a manifesto to the people of Russia, whom it addresses “Citizens.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1917: Prince Lvov Tells Nation His Policy', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-20T15:57:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0ae499d-cdec-5f0d-b97a-99e6995d603f', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0ae499d-cdec-5f0d-b97a-99e6995d603f'}, {'abstract': 'A documentary follows the chef Michael Solomonov on a journey through the country’s kitchens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/20/dining/in-search-of-israeli-cuisine-michael-solomonov.html', 'snippet': 'A documentary follows the chef Michael Solomonov on a journey through the country’s kitchens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the new feature-length documentary “In Search of Israeli Cuisine,” the chef Michael Solomonov travels from one end of Israel to the other sampling food and talking to cooks in a narrative style reminiscent of Anthony Bourdain. After watching this film, one has to conclude that with more than 100 nationalities living within the country’s borders, an Israeli cuisine resists easy definition. Many cuisines — some clearly Jewish, some not — have been validated there in recent decades. Local ingredients have found new standing, blooming even in the Negev desert. While exploring the food mosaic, the film also points out the simmering tension between Arabic and Israeli cooking. Who can claim ownership of falafel, shakshuka or chopped salad?: “In Search of Israeli Cuisine,” featuring Michael Solomonov, a production of Florentine Films/Sherman Pictures, in select theaters starting Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22BURNER-MOVIE/22BURNER-MOVIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22BURNER-MOVIE/22BURNER-MOVIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22BURNER-MOVIE/22BURNER-MOVIE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22BURNER-MOVIE/22BURNER-MOVIE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22BURNER-MOVIE/22BURNER-MOVIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22BURNER-MOVIE/22BURNER-MOVIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22BURNER-MOVIE/22BURNER-MOVIE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel’s Rich Culinary Legacy Revealed in a New Film', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel’s Food Culture Explored in New Film', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Solomonov, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zahav (Philadelphia, Pa, Restaurant)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'In Search of Israeli Cuisine (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-20T16:09:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6fac01c-2387-5fb9-8baa-73589989fd2b', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6fac01c-2387-5fb9-8baa-73589989fd2b'}, {'abstract': 'This mixer from Q Drinks is a fine match for juniper-forward gins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/20/dining/tonic-water-q-drinks.html', 'snippet': 'This mixer from Q Drinks is a fine match for juniper-forward gins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a drink calls for tonic, the quality of the mixer is as critical as that of the spirit. Q Drinks has just added a second tonic water to its line of carbonated sodas. The new Indian tonic water has a more assertive flavor profile than its regular tonic (labeled Spectacular), with more bitterness and a touch more sweetness. It’s a better foil for more juniper-forward London-style dry gins, although it works with any gin. The name is a nod to India, where tonic originated as a way to add antimalarial quinine to drinks at British officer’s clubs: Q Indian Tonic Water, sold in 6.7-ounce and 750-milliliter glass bottles in many markets, online retailers and from qdrinks.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22BURNER-TONIC/22BURNER-TONIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22BURNER-TONIC/22BURNER-TONIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22BURNER-TONIC/22BURNER-TONIC-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22BURNER-TONIC/22BURNER-TONIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22BURNER-TONIC/22BURNER-TONIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22BURNER-TONIC/22BURNER-TONIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22BURNER-TONIC/22BURNER-TONIC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a London Dry Gin, a More Assertive Tonic', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dry Gins Have a Match With This Assertive Tonic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Q Drinks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails and Mixed Drinks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name':