ion, in case you don’t want to walk barefoot across the floor. And if you’d rather sit somewhere outside the splash zone — instead of donning a poncho, perching on the edge of the pool with the rest of the audience and dangling your feet in the water — that’s allowed, too.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/21/arts/21POOLPLAY1/21POOLPLAY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/21/arts/21POOLPLAY1/21POOLPLAY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/21/arts/21POOLPLAY1/21POOLPLAY1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/21/arts/21POOLPLAY1/21POOLPLAY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/21/arts/21POOLPLAY1/21POOLPLAY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/21/arts/21POOLPLAY1/21POOLPLAY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/21/arts/21POOLPLAY1/21POOLPLAY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Pool Play 2.0,’ the Audience Is Welcome to Make a Splash', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Audience Gets Its Feet Wet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Pool Play 2.0 (Play)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'This Is Not a Theater Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mee, Charles L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matthews, Jonathan (Dancer)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mee, Erin B', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bear, Jessie', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Waterside Plaza Swim & Health Club (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-20T23:20:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Collins-Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins-Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c81ecce8-01c3-5c00-b795-6a75282a05da', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c81ecce8-01c3-5c00-b795-6a75282a05da'}, {'abstract': '“The Good Fight” is at its most political and confounding this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/20/arts/television/the-good-fight-social-media-and-its-discontents-recap.html', 'snippet': '“The Good Fight” is at its most political and confounding this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1999, Joss Whedon’s genre bending, pop feminist masterwork “Buffy the Vampire Slayer” aired “The Zeppo” in Season 3. The episode had several of the qualities that made the series an enduring cult hit, with one noticeable difference: It was told from the perspective of a sidekick, Xander Harris (Nicholas Brendon). Giving Xander his own adventure separate from the rest of the cast gave viewers a new prism through which to filter “Buffy”’s potent ideas. “The Zeppo” illustrates how different a show can be when a character that exists in the margins is brought to the center. Watching Sunday’s episode of “The Good Fight,” I couldn’t help but wonder how different an episode would be if it took on the perspective of one of the black members of the firm. If any character on “The Good Fight” deserves its very own “Zeppo” episode, it’s Barbara.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/watching/19goodfight/19goodfight-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/17/watching/19goodfight/19goodfight-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/watching/19goodfight/19goodfight-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/watching/19goodfight/20watching-slide-5FYE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/17/watching/19goodfight/20watching-slide-5FYE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 452}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/watching/19goodfight/20watching-slide-5FYE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/17/watching/19goodfight/20watching-slide-5FYE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1542, 'wi