ually result in one million more people being uninsured, according to the C.B.O.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/21/upshot/fewer-americans-would-be-insured-with-gop-plan-than-with-simple-repeal.html', 'snippet': 'The Republicans’ repeal plan of Obamacare would actually result in one million more people being uninsured, according to the C.B.O.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Congressional Budget Office recently said that around 24 million fewer Americans would have health insurance in 2026 under the Republican repeal plan than if the current law stayed in place.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fewer Americans Would Be Insured With G.O.P. Plan Than With Simple Repeal', 'kicker': 'Public Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fewer Would Be Insured With G.O.P. Plan Than With a Simple Repeal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Budget Office', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-21T16:05:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margot Sanger-Katz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margot', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanger-Katz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/035cc860-a2dd-5881-a285-aef6f268998a', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/035cc860-