 (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-21T17:19:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76cb444d-ffe1-536c-989f-56d9668d448e', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76cb444d-ffe1-536c-989f-56d9668d448e'}, {'abstract': 'After a court ruling this month, the lawyers say they left because of an internal dispute over conflicts of interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/21/business/dealbook/breakaway-lawyers-from-kasowitz-firm-point-to-conflicts-dispute.html', 'snippet': 'After a court ruling this month, the lawyers say they left because of an internal dispute over conflicts of interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A group of lawyers known for celebrity divorces surprised the legal industry last spring when they announced they would leave the New York law firm led by Marc E. Kasowitz, a longtime lawyer for President Trump, after two decades at the firm.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breakaway Lawyers From Kasowitz Firm Point to Conflicts Dispute', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Celebrity Divorce Lawyers Left Over Conflicts Dispute', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rose, Joseph B', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alter, Eleanor B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kasowitz, Marc E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-21T17:24:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Olson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7115a48f-d666-5936-9c10-27882a1f1493', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7115a48f-d666-5936-9c10-27882a1f1493'}, {'abstract': 'President Trump has empowered repressive governments around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2017/03/21/human-rights-activist-bahrain-backed-by-u-s-is-targeting-my-family/', 'snippet': 'President Trump has empowered repressive governments around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON —\xa0In early March, a group of masked men accompanied by police officers\xa0arrested\xa0my brother-in-law in Bahrain. Three days later, my mother-in-law was arrested as well. Both were charged with planting “fake bombs” and prosecutors ordered 30 days detention for them. My brother-in-law, Nazar, said the police tortured him and forced him to implicate other family members in wrongdoing. They told him they were out for revenge for actions I had taken as a human rights activist.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/opinion/20kristofblog_sayed/20kristofblog_sayed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 843, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/20/opinion/20kristofblog_sayed/20kristofblog_sayed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 843}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/opinion/20kristofblog_sayed/20kristofblog_sayed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 729, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/opinion/20kristofblog_sayed/20kristofblog_sayed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1457, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/opinion/20kristofblog_sayed/20kristofblog_sayed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/20/opinion/20kristofblog_sayed/20kristofblog_sayed-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/20/opinion/20kristofblog_sayed/20kristofblog_sayed-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Human Rights Activist: Bahrain, Backed by U.S., is Targeting My Family', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajab, Nabeel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahrain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-21T17:36:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sayed Ahmed AlWadaei', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sayed', 'middlename': 'Ahmed', 'lastname': 'AlWadaei', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b679546-b4f9-598b-b306-f06a2e77ca83', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b679546-b4f9-598b-b306-f06a2e77ca83'}, {'abstract': 'The actor and writer talks about his early days, working with Off Center Theater, where he encountered young audiences eager to see characters like themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/21/theater/john-leguizamo-the-first-time-i-faced-a-hostile-audience-kids.html', 'snippet': 'The actor and writer talks about his early days, working with Off Center Theater, where he encountered young audiences eager to see characters like themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There I was playing Jack from “Jack and the Beanstalk,” pretending to climb a rope. Suddenly — boom! — the giant comes out, and several castmates and I erupt in a synchronized breakdance, mirroring one another’s moves. The crowd screams with a mixture of joy and fear, trying to make Jack hip to the fact that he’s about to be captured. This was all in a day’s work, as I was trying to be an actor and the only gig I could get was a diverse children’s theater troupe that was hiring my flavor.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26FIRSTTIME-LEGUIZAMO-COMBO/26FIRSTTIME-LEGUIZAMO-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 275, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26FIRSTTIME-LEGUIZAMO-COMBO/26FIRSTTIME-LEGUIZAMO-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 275}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26FIRSTTIME-LEGUIZAMO-COMBO/26FIRSTTIME-LEGUIZAMO-COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 469, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26FIRSTTIME-LEGUIZAMO-COMBO/26FIRSTTIME-LEGUIZAMO-COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 939, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26FIRSTTIME-LEGUIZAMO-COMBO/26FIRSTTIME-LEGUIZAMO-COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26FIRSTTIME-LEGUIZAMO-COMBO/26FIRSTTIME-LEGUIZAMO-COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26FIRSTTIME-LEGUIZAMO-COMBO/26FIRSTTIME-LEGUIZAMO-COMBO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'John Leguizamo: The First Time I Faced a Hostile Audience (Kids)', 'kicker': 'The First Time', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '… I Faced a Hostile Audience (Kids)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leguizamo, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'val