b58b552d-242d-5b75-a33c-962b8261b390', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/b58b552d-242d-5b75-a33c-962b8261b390'}, {'abstract': 'Who is affected by the flight restriction, and what should you do?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/21/technology/personaltech/what-travelers-should-know-about-new-restrictions-on-devices.html', 'snippet': 'Who is affected by the flight restriction, and what should you do?', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — The United States Department of Homeland Security on Tuesday enacted a new flight restriction. Under the rule, passengers traveling on foreign airlines from eight majority-Muslim countries to the United States are barred from bringing devices larger than cellphones onto the plane. Instead, they have to stow devices like computers and tablets in checked luggage.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/business/22DEVICES1/22DEVICES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/22/business/22DEVICES1/22DEVICES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/business/22DEVICES1/22DEVICES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/business/22DEVICES1/22DEVICES1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/business/22DEVICES1/22DEVICES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/22/business/22DEVICES1/22DEVICES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/business/22DEVICES1/22DEVICES1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Travelers Should Know About New Restrictions on Devices', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Questions and Answers on a New Restriction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-21T19:10:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48860577-4879-5487-8bfe-cfb5fe8128b8', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48860577-4879-5487-8bfe-cfb5fe8128b8'}, {'abstract': 'A move by James Kent, Masa Takayama’s non-sushi project moves forward, and other restaurant news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/21/dining/alex-stupak-empellon-midtown-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'A move by James Kent, Masa Takayama’s non-sushi project moves forward, and other restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EMPELLÓN Having spent six years establishing a group of downtown restaurants, each with a different focus but all bearing the Empellón name, Alex Stupak is ready to unveil what will be his flagship, in Midtown. “I’m treating Midtown like a neighborhood, and hope to cater to the needs and tastes of the people who work and live here,” he said. A two-level restaurant serving Mexican food in a shiny new office building is hardly cookie-cutter Midtown, but Mr. Stupak is counting on his approach to the cuisine, filled unapologetically with American and other influences — he makes no claim to authenticity — appealing to the Midtown set. “Everyone told me that I had to have a shrimp cocktail in Midtown,” he said. “I didn’t think so.” Instead, his freewheeling menu offers starters like crab nachos with sea urchin, chopped cabbage salad with toasted dried fava bean dressing, and nine different tacos, including a falafel one and another with spit-roasted beef that is a take on al pastor. “We’re using tacos as a gateway drug to get people to try other stuff,” he said. Some larger plates, including roasted red prawns with chipotle, and fajitas with black pepper mole, round out the choices. The design for the 150-seat space, by Glen Coben in collaboration with Mr. Stupak, is airy and bright, with a big bar area and a more intimate dining room and open kitchen beyond. Upstairs, there are tables on the overhanging balcony and several private rooms. All are adorned with Mexican art pieces. (Opens Thursday): 510 Madison Avenue (53rd Street), 212-858-9365, empellon.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22OFF/22OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22OFF/22OFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22OFF/22OFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22OFF/22OFF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22OFF/22OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22OFF/22OFF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/dining/22OFF/22OFF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alex Stupak Unveils His Empellón Flagship in Midtown Manhattan', 'kicker': 'Off the Menu', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Empellon (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stupak, Alex', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Luke's Lobster (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Bobby Van's", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-21T19:21:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fc7f2ff-c028-59db-a754-520aa9394383', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fc7f2ff-c028-59db-a754-520aa9394383'}, {'abstract': 'The artist has created an entirely reflective structure just outside of Palm Springs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/21/t-magazine/art/doug-aitken-desert-x-mirage-ranch-house.html', 'snippet': 'The artist has created an entirely reflective structure just outside of Palm Springs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Set into the side of a boulder-strewn mountain, overlooking the point where the city of Palm Springs, Calif., intersects with raw, untouched desert, sits an empty suburban ranch house clad entirely in mirrors — a kind of life-size kaleidoscope that blends landscape and sky. But instead of being an actual home, the structure is an installation called “Mirage” by the artist Doug Aitken.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watch Doug Aitken’s Mirrored Ranch House Transform Over Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deserts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aitken, Doug', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-21T19:24:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Orton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Orton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaac5ae8-1d57-5afa-96c7-7659f7dda367', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaac5ae8-1d57-5afa-96c7-7659f7dda367'}, {'abstract': 'Corporate messages of self-care tend to preach idleness. I’m suspicious.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/21/opinion/work-is-my-self-care.html', 'snippet': 'Corporate messages of self-care tend to preach idleness. I’m suspicious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day in mid-November, I followed a crowd of teenagers from Trump Tower to Washington Square Park in the pouring rain. They were protesting President Trump’s election and I was writing about them. In order to talk to as many kids as possible, I kept running ahead in the protest, falling behind as I walked with a group, then running ahead again. By the time I reached the park I was wet to the skin, but I could’ve run fifty more blocks. I was happier than I’d been in weeks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/21northWeb/21northWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/21northWeb/21northWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/21northWeb/21northWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/21northWeb/21northWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/21northWeb/21northWeb-thum