'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelosi, Nancy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Takano, Mark A', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Linda T', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-22T00:43:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Qiu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Qiu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e8a89fc-49d1-5cc3-aa91-162169f01050', 'word_count': 1139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e8a89fc-49d1-5cc3-aa91-162169f01050'}, {'abstract': 'The G.O.P. has no coherent idea or shared vision of what it wants to achieve, aside from killing Obamacare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/21/opinion/a-republican-health-care-bill-in-search-of-a-problem.html', 'snippet': 'The G.O.P. has no coherent idea or shared vision of what it wants to achieve, aside from killing Obamacare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republican leaders in the House have been huddling over the last few days in a frantic search for enough votes to win passage of their proposed revision of Obamacare, in the process making an already flawed bill even worse. One measure of their desperation was a cynical last-minute provision that would shift Medicaid costs from New York’s rural and suburban counties to the state government, pleasing upstate Republicans who represent those counties but reducing coverage provided by the state.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/22wed1/22wed1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 532, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/22wed1/22wed1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 532}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/22wed1/22wed1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 908, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/22wed1/22wed1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1445, 'width': 1630, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/22wed1/22wed1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/22wed1/22wed1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/22wed1/22wed1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Republican Health Care Bill in Search of a Problem', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republican Health Care Confusion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-22T00:53:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ba1e46a-2b5d-53cc-85c1-89a3be6e5a10', 'word_count': 569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ba1e46a-2b5d-53cc-85c1-89a3be6e5a10'}, {'abstract': 'In clinging to wiretap claims, the president draws on his history as a pugnacious fighter, with a need to prove his legitimacy and a deep sensitivity to perception.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/21/us/politics/trump-obama-wiretapping-motivation.html', 'snippet': 'In clinging to wiretap claims, the president draws on his history as a pugnacious fighter, with a need to prove his legitimacy and a deep sensitivity to perception.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Trump is a man seriously susceptible to snagging himself in the nettles of obsession. In the last three weeks, no compulsion has so consumed his psyche, and his Twitter account, as the deeply held and shallowly sourced belief that President Barack Obama tapped his phones.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/us/22trumpwhy/22trumpwhy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/22/us/22trumpwhy