ve Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-22T08:57:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Mozur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mozur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55a196a4-80de-5a4e-bdf2-d7d315a57191', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55a196a4-80de-5a4e-bdf2-d7d315a57191'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on whether to preserve a historical artifact with a troubling history and whether scholarship funds should be only for the neediest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/22/magazine/what-should-you-do-with-your-fathers-nazi-keepsake.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on whether to preserve a historical artifact with a troubling history and whether scholarship funds should be only for the neediest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few years ago, before my father died, my two brothers and I were going through his things with him. He wanted to have some say in where his belongings went. We agreeably found a home for most of the things: Brother No. 2 has children; Brother No. 3 and I have no children. When it came to my father’s World War II box, which had not been opened for years, we thought it best to give his Bronze Star, Purple Heart and other military decorations to Brother No. 2, so they could be passed down.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26ethicist/26mag-26ethicist-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 415, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26ethicist/26mag-26ethicist-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 415, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26ethicist/26mag-26ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26ethicist/26mag-26ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26ethicist/26mag-26ethicist-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Should You Do With Your Father’s Nazi Keepsake?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Should I Do With My Father’s Nazi Keepsake?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memorabilia and Souvenirs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grants (Corporate and Foundation)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tutors and Tutoring', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-22T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42ad77f4-8776-50d7-9d6e-91ba71baa715', 'word_count': 1319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42ad77f4-8776-50d7-9d6e-91ba71baa715'}, {'abstract': 'The host of CNN’s “Believer” on converting from and back to Islam and why watching TV is so important.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/22/magazine/reza-aslan-thinks-tv-can-end-bigotry.html', 'snippet': 'The host of CNN’s “Believer” on converting from and back to Islam and why watching TV is so important.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On your new show, “Believer,” you examine niche, sometimes extreme, global religious traditions. Do you think this is the best time for a show like this? It is the most perfect time possible. There is no medium on this earth that has more power to transform the way that people think about others than television.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '94', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26talk/26mag-26talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26talk/26mag-26talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26talk/26mag-26talk-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26talk/26mag-26talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26talk/26mag-26talk-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1370}}, {'rank': 0, 'sub