aph': 'I used to think there were two types of people in this world: those who are so nervous about making their flight that they are only truly happy if they get to the airport four hours early, and those who are so blasé about making their flight that they are only truly happy if they get to the airport just minutes before takeoff.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/travel/26ESSAYAIRPORT/26ESSAYAIRPORT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/26/travel/26ESSAYAIRPORT/26ESSAYAIRPORT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/travel/26ESSAYAIRPORT/26ESSAYAIRPORT-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/travel/26ESSAYAIRPORT/26ESSAYAIRPORT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 208, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/26/travel/26ESSAYAIRPORT/26ESSAYAIRPORT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 208}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/travel/26ESSAYAIRPORT/26ESSAYAIRPORT-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/travel/26ESSAYAIRPORT/26ESSAYAIRPORT-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Security Lines and Flight Delays? This Kid’s in Paradise', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Security Lines and Flight Delays? He’s in Paradise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-22T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reif Larsen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reif', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Larsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acb2a771-a6fb-5675-9121-62afeec130eb', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acb2a771-a6fb-5675-9121-62afeec130eb'}, {'abstract': 'This gargantuan shrine to democracy has never felt so surreal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/22/magazine/why-does-mount-rushmore-exist.html', 'snippet': 'This gargantuan shrine to democracy has never felt so surreal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nothing about our trip to Mount Rushmore went according to plan. Our flight was delayed. We found ourselves stranded in the Minneapolis airport for four hours. “Minneapolis airport four hours,” we typed into Google, and the internet responded by persuading us to take a train to the Mall of America. The entrance was shabby; the elevators were slow and small and confusing; locals walked around in the freezing weather wearing short sleeves. It was not just a mall but an elaborate fun house of malls — malls within malls within malls within malls — at the center of which was, somehow, a gigantic amusement park. My children watched in jealous awe as another family floated by on a log ride. I could see their child-minds recalibrating the relative scales and possibilities of American experience. How big could one thing be while still fitting inside another?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '38', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26rushmore4/26rushmore4-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26rushmore4/26rushmore4-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26rushmore4/26rushmore4-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26rushmore4/26rushmore4-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1357, 'width': 2035, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26rushmore4/26rushmore4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26rushmore4/26rushmore4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/magazine/26rushmore4/26rushmore4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Does Mount Rushmore Exist?', 'kicker': 'The Voyages Issue', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peak America', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mall of America (Bloomington, Minn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mount Rushmore National Memorial (SD)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-22T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Anderson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Anderson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e198eba1-6fc8-5662-bb97-5574707b215d', 'word_count': 3521, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e198eba1-6fc8-5662-bb97-5574707b215d'}, {'abstract': 'Joining up with the Great Loop, an intricate route that transforms half the United States into an island.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/22/magazine/an-improbable-6000-mile-boat-trip-around-the-east-coast.html', 'snippet': 'Joining up with the Great Loop, an intricate route that transforms half the United States into an island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before I set sail with Tim and Karen Bartel on their 52-foot Bluewater yacht, Let It Ride, I didn’t tend to think of water as a place. I learned my geography by that wooden map of the United States — the jigsaw puzzle of the lower 48 with the inset Hawaii and Alaska to the side. The puzzle-piece states were the places to go, and everything else was just negative space. You could not visit the compass rose in the corner, nor the unvarnished pine off the coast of Oahu. The winding Mississippi and proboscoid Great Lakes gave shape to the puzzle but didn’t qualify as destinations themselves. In a nation transfixed by the dream of the road trip, a river is just a reason for a tunnel or a bridge