 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tep Khunnal', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-22T13:42:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Wallace', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wallace', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4fff6ea-b01d-59bb-839d-604b420eb25d', 'word_count': 1154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4fff6ea-b01d-59bb-839d-604b420eb25d'}, {'abstract': 'The pop star and actress served as an executive producer with her mother to adapt a novel into a show about isolation and adolescent suicide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/22/arts/television/selena-gomez-thirteen-reasons-why-netflix.html', 'snippet': 'The pop star and actress served as an executive producer with her mother to adapt a novel into a show about isolation and adolescent suicide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEST HOLLYWOOD, Calif. — In 2008, Mandy Teefey, the mother of the pop star and actress Selena Gomez, was browsing at a Barnes & Noble when she spotted “Thirteen Reasons Why” by Jay Asher. The best-selling young adult novel tells the story of Hannah Baker, a high school girl who kills herself, leaving behind cassette tapes detailing the 13 people she blames for driving her to suicide. It’s no surprise that, standing in the bookstore, Ms. Teefey was compelled to read it: Woven into Hannah’s dark account of isolation, adolescent betrayal and sexual stigmatizing are messages of acceptance and compassion, yet it unfolds like an emotional thriller. Not much later, Ms. Teefey and Ms. Gomez were eating sushi with Mr. Asher, negotiating for the rights.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26GOMEZ1/26GOMEZ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 489, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26GOMEZ1/26GOMEZ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 489}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26GOMEZ1/26GOMEZ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26GOMEZ1/26GOMEZ1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1668, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26GOMEZ1/26GOMEZ1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26GOMEZ1/26GOMEZ1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26GOMEZ1/26GOMEZ1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Selena Gomez (and Others) on Adapting ‘Thirteen Reasons Why’ for Netflix', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saving Lives, One Episode at a Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': '13 Reasons Why (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gomez, Selena', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teefey, Mandy', '