nd Latino students out of some of the city’s best schools.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/22/opinion/the-truth-about-new-york-citys-elite-high-schools.html', 'snippet': 'Bad policy and a false narrative of inferiority are keeping black and Latino students out of some of the city’s best schools.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This month, a select group of eighth graders in New York City found out that they were being offered a spot at some of the nation’s best high schools, the eight “specialized” city public high schools that include Stuyvesant High School, Brooklyn Tech and Bronx Science. About 28,000 students took the multiple-choice test required for admission, and 5,078 did well enough to secure a place.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/22hewittWeb/22hewittWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/22hewittWeb/22hewittWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/22hewittWeb/22hewittWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/22hewittWeb/22hewittWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1265, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/22hewittWeb/22hewittWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/22/opinion/22hewittWeb/22hewittWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth'