pe': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Coscarelli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coscarelli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85425ebe-3ad2-51bd-ad60-db298cf81b5d', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85425ebe-3ad2-51bd-ad60-db298cf81b5d'}, {'abstract': 'The company celebrates its 30th anniversary season with three works: “Folded,” “ReComposed” and “Possession.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/22/arts/dance/doug-varone-and-dancers-swirl-into-the-brooklyn-academy-of-music.html', 'snippet': 'The company celebrates its 30th anniversary season with three works: “Folded,” “ReComposed” and “Possession.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Doug Varone’s dances swirl with steps, and those propulsive steps swirl with ideas and emotions. Just consider the ever-shifting kinetic imagery in the three works being presented by Doug Varone and Dancers in performances at Brooklyn Academy of Music beginning Wednesday, March 29, as part of the company’s 30th anniversary season. The movements in “Folded,” an intimate duet, unfold with questions about — and contradictions in — personal beliefs and behavior. The restlessness of “ReComposed” pays tribute to the vivid hues and bold brush strokes of Joan Mitchell, an American abstract expressionist artist whose paintings can seem like whirlwinds of color. And “Possession” is inspired by the changing relationships in A. S. Byatt’s novel of the same name, in which two contemporary literary scholars find themselves increasingly caught up in the emotional predicaments of the two Victorian poets whose personal lives they are researching. (Through April 1, Harvey Theater, Fort Greene; bam.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26GUIDE3/26GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26GUIDE3/26GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26GUIDE3/26GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26GUIDE3/26GUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1260, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26GUIDE3/26GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26GUIDE3/26GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/arts/26GUIDE3/26GUIDE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Doug Varone and Dancers Swirl Into the Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dance; Spinning Kinetic Imagery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Varone, Doug, and Dancers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-22T15:18:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'new