cio De Alba has been photographing women who — like her — have confronted their substance abuse to lead fulfilling, if challenging, lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once she got sober,\xa0Rocio De Alba\xa0began noticing women trying to stop drinking or using drugs\xa0everywhere she looked. She saw them on the news, interviewed in decrepit halfway houses. She saw them in documentaries, caught in alleys and corners dying for a fix — and dying to stop. She studied their close-ups in photo essays, their faces creased and spotted, roadmaps of their worst days.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Women in Recovery, One Photo at a Time', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Group Homes and Supportive Housing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'De Alba, Rocio', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-23T08:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn Nieves', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nieves', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96fd263a-e41a-5db5-adf8-98bf57c38635', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96fd263a-e41a-5db5-adf8-98bf57c38635'}, {'abstract': 'The Islamic State claimed responsibility for the attack carried out by Khalid Masood, 52, who had a criminal record but was not on any police-monitoring lists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/23