though in good health, he can foresee a time when he won’t be a confident driver, if he can drive at all. While he hopes to continue to live in his suburban Detroit home, he wonders how he will be able to get to places like his doctor’s office and the supermarket if his driving becomes impaired.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/24/business/24WHEELS/24WHEELS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/24/business/24WHEELS/24WHEELS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/24/business/24WHEELS/24WHEELS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/24/business/24WHEELS/24WHEELS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1381, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/24/business/24WHEELS/24WHEELS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/24/business/24WHEELS/24WHEELS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/24/business/24WHEELS/24WHEELS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Self-Driving Cars Could Be Boon for Aged, After Initial Hurdles', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For the Aged, Self-Driving Cars Could Bridge a Mobility Gap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Driverless and Semiautonomous Vehicles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-23T15:11:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'Wheels', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary M. Chapman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72e54ba7-3f12-5949-a8d0-685f31cac890', 'word_count': 1065, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72e54ba7-3f12-5949-a8d0-685f31cac890'}, {'abstract': 'Brides and grooms do whatever they can to steady their nerves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/23/fashion/weddings/got-wedding-jitters-.html', 'snippet': 'Brides and grooms do whatever they can to steady their nerves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For her wedding, Hannah Spinrad welcomed 250 guests to Greensboro, N.C., her hometown, on Memorial Day weekend last year. The guests stayed at the 1,500-acre Grandover Resort and enjoyed a stream of activities, from a golf tournament to snacking in the hospitality suite. The bride was always there to ensure that details were executed flawlessly and that guests were mingling and happy.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/fashion/26JITTERS/26JITTERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/26/fashion/26JITTERS/26JITTERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 470}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'captio