/article/ba409ee4-53dc-5b2a-82f0-ee6eb285bdfc'}, {'abstract': 'The extension, which will keep Mr. Iger at Disney until 2019, reflected the difficulty the company has had identifying a successor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/23/business/media/robert-iger-disneys-ceo-agrees-to-one-year-extension.html', 'snippet': 'The extension, which will keep Mr. Iger at Disney until 2019, reflected the difficulty the company has had identifying a successor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Robert A. Iger has extended his reign at the Magic Kingdom for a third time, as an heir continues to be difficult to find.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Robert Iger, Disney’s C.E.O., Agrees to One-Year Extension', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Successor Yet to Be Found, Disney’s C.E.O. Will Stay On Another Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iger, Robert A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-23T16:06:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9afd9ec-21d3-55ed-b31f-5992da6d5ac2', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9afd9ec-21d3-55ed-b31f-5992da6d5ac2'}, {'abstract': 'Pew surveys also show people disagree on whether it should be mandatory or optional.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/23/upshot/americans-agree-on-paid-leave-but-not-on-who-should-pay.html', 'snippet': 'Pew surveys also show people disagree on whether it should be mandatory or optional.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most people say workers should get paid leave to take care of a baby, a sick family member or themselves, according to two new surveys. But they disagree on the details: who should pay, and whether it should be mandatory or optional.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/23/upshot/24up-paidleave2/24up-paidleave2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/23/upshot/24up-paidleave2/24up-paidleave2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/23/upshot/24up-paidleave2/24up-paidleave2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/23/upshot/24up-paidleave2/24up-paidleave2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/23/upshot/24up-paidleave2/24up-paidleave2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/23/upshot/24up-paidleave2/24up-paidleave2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/23/upshot/24up-paidleave2/24up-paidleave2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Americans Agree on Paid Leave, but Not on Who Should Pay', 'kicker': 'Survey Says', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Americans Agree on Paid Leave, but Not on Who Should Pay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paid Time Off', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Leaves', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-23T16:10:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41a0e588-4e0c-5595-b389-def385c451dd', 'word_count': 1069, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41a0e588-4e0c-5595-b389-def385c451dd'}, {'abstract': 'Kinsey Wilson, the executive vice president of product and technology, responds to reader concerns about efforts to tailor Times content.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/23/public-editor/whyd-do-you-that-kinsey-wilson-liz-spayd.html', 'snippet': 'Kinsey Wilson, the executive vice president of product and technology, responds to reader concerns about efforts to tailor Times content.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I received many emails and comments from readers on my last column about The Times’s efforts to better tailor the presentation of its content toward individual preferences. At the suggestion of several of you, I asked Kinsey Wilson, the executive vice president of product and technology and editor for innovation and strategy, to respond to some of your concerns. Here is what he wrote in its entirety. Thank you all for expressing your views, and thank you, Kinsey, for addressing reader questions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/sunday-review/19PubEd/19PubEd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/19/sunday-review/19PubEd/19PubEd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/sunday-review/19PubEd/19PubEd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/sunday-review/19PubEd/19PubEd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/19/sunday-review/19PubEd/19PubEd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 771}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/sunday-review/19PubEd/19PubEd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 797, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/19/sunday-review/19PubEd/19PubEd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1593, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why’d Do You That? Individualizing The News', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Kinsey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-23T16:14:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Public Editor', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Spayd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spayd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/84454386-689c-514f-98e7-1bf83079f9c6', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84454386-689c-514f-98e7-1bf83079f9c6'}, {'abstract': 'Also, a cash-bar conundrum, a delayed apology for flaking and an infantilizing boss.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/23/fashion/car-pool-girls-puberty-birthday-cash-bar-saying-sorry-too-late.html', 'snippet': 'Also, a cash-bar conundrum, a delayed apology for flaking and an infantilizing boss.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I take turns driving my 12-year-old daughter, who is very small for her age, in a car pool with two friends from her class. One is extremely tall and skinny, the other is average height but developing breasts earlier than the others. They all look so uncomfortable in their skin. The tall girl walks hunched over, and the one with breasts rounds her shoulders to hide them. My daughter begs for heels. I’d like to say something supportive. Or is that exceeding my rights as a car-pool mom?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima