rainspotting,” the Scottish Renton (Ewan McGregor) and Simon (Jonny Lee Miller) have made their way to a loyalist club (where members are often opposed to the Roman Catholic Church) to steal customers’ credit cards. As they make their escape, they are cornered and made to go onstage to perform a song. They improvise and come up with a bit of sectarian musicianship they hope will appease their Protestant crowd.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Danny Boyle Narrates a Scene From ‘T2 Trainspotting’', 'kicker': 'Anatomy of a Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'T2 Trainspotting (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boyle, Danny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGregor, Ewan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Johnny Lee', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-23T20:38:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ac2fa8c-b5f4-569e-9280-fd6a17aad77a', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ac2fa8c-b5f4-569e-9280-fd6a17aad77a'}, {'abstract': 'This essay collection finds a firebrand author railing against modern feminism and groupthink at American universities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/23/books/review-camille-paglia-free-women-free-men.html', 'snippet': 'This essay collection finds a firebrand author railing against modern feminism and groupthink at American universities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FREE WOMEN, FREE MENSex, Gender, Femini