'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/14560910-4603-55a1-8ea4-fd834e5c5b4f', 'word_count': 838, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14560910-4603-55a1-8ea4-fd834e5c5b4f'}, {'abstract': 'What is behind the fascination with the real-life connections between an author and her work?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/23/books/review/stop-reading-my-fiction-as-the-story-of-my-life.html', 'snippet': 'What is behind the fascination with the real-life connections between an author and her work?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The panic starts in London. I’m there publicizing my last book, and at a small press lunch, my British publicist tells me that she’s just read the novel I’ve recently finished writing. She leans close to me and says, quietly, “You should prepare yourself for invasive publicity.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/books/review/0326-BKS-AuthorsNote/0326-BKS-AuthorsNote-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/26/books/review/0326-BKS-AuthorsNote/0326-BKS-AuthorsNote-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/books/review/0326-BKS-AuthorsNote/0326-BKS-AuthorsNote-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/books/review/0326-BKS-AuthorsNote/0326-BKS-AuthorsNote-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 798, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy':