i': 'nyt://article/4ec89792-187f-51e6-8b50-bc517b2f408b'}, {'abstract': 'In a new Hemingway biography, “Writer, Sailor, Soldier, Spy,” the historian Nicholas Reynolds details his subject’s work for a precursor to the K.G.B.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/24/books/review/the-great-american-novelist-who-spied-for-the-soviets.html', 'snippet': 'In a new Hemingway biography, “Writer, Sailor, Soldier, Spy,” the historian Nicholas Reynolds details his subject’s work for a precursor to the K.G.B.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Old Man And The C.C.C.P.: The military historian Nicholas Reynolds considers himself a lifelong fan of Ernest Hemingway. “I started reading Hemingway when I was in junior high,” he told me in a recent email exchange, and even at that precocious age he admired all the things you might expect a future military historian to admire in Hemingway’s work. “The characters he created embodied so many American values we still cherish,” Reynolds explains in the introduction to his new Hemingway biography, “Writer, Sailor, Soldier, Spy,” which enters the hardcover nonfiction list at No.\u202f14. “Truth, bravery, independence, grace under pressure, standing up for the underdog.” ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/24/books/review/24reynolds/24reynolds-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 271, 'width': 259, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/24/books/review/24reynolds/24reynolds-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 271, 'width': 259, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/24/books/review/24reynolds/24reynolds-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, '