: 'Insider', 'section_name': 'Times Insider', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/455e47e7-1369-5487-9f55-a477a3173605', 'word_count': 1216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/455e47e7-1369-5487-9f55-a477a3173605'}, {'abstract': 'Emerging from the torpor of winter means a busy spring for these bears, bees, bats and squirrels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/24/science/hibernation-spring-bears-bees-bats-arctic-squirrels.html', 'snippet': 'Emerging from the torpor of winter means a busy spring for these bears, bees, bats and squirrels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For animals that hibernate, making it to spring is no small feat. Torpor — the state of reduced bodily activity that occurs during hibernation — is not restful. By the time they emerge, hibernating animals are often sleep-deprived: Most expend huge bursts of energy to arouse themselves occasionally in the winter so their body temperatures don’t dip too low. This back-and-forth is exhausting, and hibernators do it with little to no food and water. By winter’s end, some have shed more than half their body weight.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/25/science/25tb-hibernation-top/25tb-hibernation-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 477, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/25/science/25tb-hibernation-top/25tb-hibernation-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 477}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/25/science/25tb-hibernation-top/25tb-hibernation-top-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 814, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/25/science/25tb-hibernation-top/25tb-hibernation-top-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1628, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/25/science/25tb-hibernation-top/25tb-hibernation-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/25/science/25tb-hibernation-top/25tb-hibernation-top-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/25/science/25tb-hibernation-top/25tb-hibernation-top-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Waking From Hibernation, the Hard Work of Spring Begins', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spring Awakening: A Fitful, Groggy End to Hibernation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hibernation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spring (Season)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seasons and Months', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bears', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bats', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Squirrels', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-24T22:38:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steph Yin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steph', 'middlenam