, {'abstract': 'Farhad and Mike discuss how YouTube’s issues with brands pulling ads because of racist content has caused a major headache for Google’s video arm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/25/technology/farhads-and-mikes-week-in-tech-youtubes-problematic-advertising.html', 'snippet': 'Farhad and Mike discuss how YouTube’s issues with brands pulling ads because of racist content has caused a major headache for Google’s video arm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each Saturday, Farhad Manjoo and Mike Isaac, technology reporters at The New York Times, review the week’s news, offering analysis and maybe a joke or two about the most important developments in the tech industry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Farhad’s and Mike’s Week in Tech: YouTube’s Problematic Advertising', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-25T13:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Farhad Manjoo and Mike Isaac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Farhad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Manjoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isaac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72e2d76f-3576-5c07-bc9f-e84a170a9444', 'word_count': 1079, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72e2d76f-3576-5c07-bc9f-e84a170a9444'}, {'abstract': 'When a tenant in a rent-stabilized building refuses to stop having loud all-night parties, what can the neighbors do?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/25/realestate/endless-parties-next-door.html', 'snippet': 'When a tenant in a rent-stabilized building refuses to stop having loud all-night parties, what can the neighbors do?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. I live in a rent-stabilized building in Chelsea, Manhattan, next to a  woman who gives  loud parties. She and her guests yell, bang on  walls and slam doors until 5 a.m. The police will not intervene because she will not open the door for them. After I complained, she retaliated by banging on my door, which I considered harassment. Many tenants, and the live-in super, have complained to her and notified the landlord, who said there is nothing he can do. Is this  true? What legal standing do we have?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/realestate/26SUBASK/26SUBASK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 109, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/26/realestate/26SUBASK/26SUBASK-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 109}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/realestate/26SUBASK/26SUBASK-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 186, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/realestate/26SUBASK/26SUBASK-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/realestate/26SUBASK/26SUBASK-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/26/realestate/26SUBASK/26SUBASK-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/realestate/26SUBASK/26SUBASK-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Endless Parties Next Door', 'kicker': 'Ask Real Estate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Noisy Neighbor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Noise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-25T14:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcd1f4a4-f077-51fb-aafb-07272281598e', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcd1f4a4-f077-51fb-aafb-07272281598e'}, {'abstract': 'Noah, who has been sidelined with a knee injury, was suspended for 20 games, starting with the first game he is physically able to play.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/25/sports/basketball/knicks-joakim-noah-suspended-for-failing-a-doping-test.html', 'snippet': 'Noah, who has been sidelined with a knee injury, was suspended for 20 games, starting with the first game he is physically able to play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Knicks’ Joakim Noah became one of the rare prominent N.B.A. players to be suspended under the league’s policy on performance-enhancing drugs when the league announced Saturday that he would serve a 20-game penalty.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia