 came to us “acquainted with grief.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'These days I find I’m more alert to the grief and sorrow around me than I once was. In part it’s a product of my age, of youth giving way. I’m guessing my situation is not that different from many of yours.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/opinion/sunday/26wehner/26wehner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 558, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/26/opinion/sunday/26wehner/26wehner-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 558}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/opinion/sunday/26wehner/26wehner-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 952, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/opinion/sunday/26wehner/26wehner-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1313, 'width': 1413, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/opinion/sunday/26wehner/26wehner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/26/opinion/sunday/26wehner/26wehner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/opinion/sunday/26wehner/26wehner-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Great Pain, Where Is God?', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Great Pain, Where Is God?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, C S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-25T18:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Wehner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wehner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/451a8644-d7af-5b17-aa0a-d3581953de56', 'word_count': 1253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/451a8644-d7af-5b17-aa0a-d3581953de56'}, {'abstract': 'The presidency of Donald Trump doesn’t spell the end of criminal justice reform. It may just be getting started.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/25/opinion/sunday/justice-springs-eternal.html', 'snippet': 'The presidency of Donald Trump doesn’t spell the end of criminal justice reform. It may just be getting started.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THIS wasn’t how the story was supposed to end. After almost 50 years of relentless prison-building in the United States, of aggressive policing and a war on drugs that goes after our most vulnerable citizens, the movement for a more merciful criminal justice system had begun to seem, if not unstoppable, at least plenty powerful.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/26/opinion/sunday/26formanWEB/26formanWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 586, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/26/opinion/sunday/26formanWEB/26forma