e_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/77f8fd92-178e-5973-9f97-303729351f6d', 'word_count': 1407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77f8fd92-178e-5973-9f97-303729351f6d'}, {'abstract': 'Pierre Thiam, a chef from Senegal, will demonstrate how to use this high-protein grain at the Museum of Food and Drink.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/27/dining/fonio-grain-pierre-thiam-talk-mofad.html', 'snippet': 'Pierre Thiam, a chef from Senegal, will demonstrate how to use this high-protein grain at the Museum of Food and Drink.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the ancient grains that has not yet made it into your granola is fonio, a finely textured high-protein member of the millet family. The West African grain can be used for soups and baking, in porridge or as a starch like polenta. Pierre Thiam, a chef and a native of Senegal, will discuss its use and demonstrate African cooking at the Museum of Food and Drink in Brooklyn: African Culinary Traditions, $30, Thursday, from 6:30 to 8 p.m. at the Museum of Food and Drink, 62 Bayard Street (Lorimer Street), Williamsburg, Brooklyn, 718-387-2845, mofad.org.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/dining/29BURNER-GRAIN/29BURNER-GRAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/29/dining/29BURNER-GRAIN/29BURNER-GRAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/dining/29BURNER-GRAIN/29BURNER-GRAIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/dining/29BURNER-GRAIN/29BURNER-GRAIN-superJu