ial': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28ccd71a-d9dc-54ff-b633-4e27a22c4348', 'word_count': 1385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28ccd71a-d9dc-54ff-b633-4e27a22c4348'}, {'abstract': 'Nine unusual powdered spices from Shed, in Healdsburg, Calif., add flavor to sauces and dips.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/27/dining/shed-healdsburg-seasoning-powders.html', 'snippet': 'Nine unusual powdered spices from Shed, in Healdsburg, Calif., add flavor to sauces and dips.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shed, a restaurant and market in Healdsburg, Calif., now sells its wares online. Along with kitchen goods, garden tools and pantry foods, the company offers nine colorful seasoning powders, some made from ingredients grown on the Shed farm. Dust the powders on poached fish, soups or deviled eggs, or use them to season sauces and dips. The green garlic powder is musky, niçoise olive is crumbly and assertive, and smoked onion harbors a sweet edge. While the shiitake mushroom powder is bland, the jade-green Padrón pepper powder is vegetal with a kick — dynamite in the place of salt on the rim of a margarita glass: Shed Powders, $15 each, healdsburgshed.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/dining/29BURNER-SEASONINGS/29BURNER-SEASONINGS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/29/dining/29BURNER-SEASONINGS/29BURNER-SEASONINGS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/dining/29BURNER-SEASONINGS/29BURNER-SEASONINGS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images