lue': 'English Language', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic National Committee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Podesta, John D', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-28T09:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Hess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2976cfde-99da-5a05-896e-2f88082813cd', 'word_count': 1423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2976cfde-99da-5a05-896e-2f88082813cd'}, {'abstract': 'A comedic structure stretches how we imagine the agonies of love.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/28/magazine/new-sentences-from-night-sky-with-exit-wounds-by-ocean-vuong.html', 'snippet': 'A comedic structure stretches how we imagine the agonies of love.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is one of stand-up comedy’s purest structures: X is so Y it’s Z — in which Y is an adjective (fat, lazy, tall, poor) and Z is some extreme consequence of that adjective. Rodney Dangerfield worked the form the way Shakespeare worked sonnets. “We were so poor, in my neighborhood the rainbow was in black and white.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/02/magazine/02sentences/02sentences-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/04/02/magazine/02sentences/02sentences-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 631}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/02/magazine/02sentences/02sentences-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 759, '