e increasingly taking up this traditional masculine pastime, looking to connect with nature and the food chain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOLMESTRAND, Norway — Shotgun at her side, Stine Hagtveldt Viddal stops at a bare patch of ground in this valley, which is thick with pine trees, pointing to the spot where she helped hunt and then skin a roe deer a few weeks ago. Taking out her phone, she shows a photo of herself holding the animal’s heart in the palm of her hand, then another of the meal she made from it later that day.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/28/world/europe/00Norway-slide-MXU2/00Norway-slide-MXU2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/02/28/world/europe/00Norway-slide-MXU2/00Norway-slide-MXU2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/28/world/europe/00Norway-slide-MXU2/00Norway-slide-MXU2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/28/world/europe/00Norway-slide-MXU2/00Norway-slide-MXU2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1344, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/02/28/world/europe/00Norway-slide-MXU2/00Norway-slide-MXU2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/02/28/world/europe/00Norway-slide-MXU2/00Norway-slide-MXU2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}},