ungest-is-66.html', 'snippet': 'Larissa Velez-Jackson, half of the duo Yackez, is bringing 11 women, ages 66 to 87, from her parallel life as a fitness instructor, into a new show.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Keep the arms heavy, feel the weight of the step,” the choreographer Larissa Velez-Jackson called to her performers, a group of women ages 66 to 87, as they practiced walking like runway models in a studio at New York Live Arts. Every few steps, they paused as if posing for a camera, throwing sultry glances toward the front of the room.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/arts/29YACKEZ1/29YACKEZ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/29/arts/29YACKEZ1/29YACKEZ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/arts/29YACKEZ1/29YACKEZ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/arts/29YACKEZ1/29YACKEZ1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/arts/29YACKEZ1/29YACKEZ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/29/arts/29YACKEZ1/29YACKEZ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/arts/29YACKEZ1/29YACKEZ1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dance Troupe Adds Fresh Faces. The Youngest Is 66.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Senior Aerobics Class to the Stage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Velez-Jackson, Larissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Velez-Jackson, Jon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yackez', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Live Arts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-28T21:07:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d310ff2c-cf05-56f8-aaf5-784f0ee6b2d2', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d310ff2c-cf05-56f8-aaf5-784f0ee6b2d2'}, {'abstract': 'The “Glee” actor and best-selling author, whose latest young adult novel is “Stranger Than Fanfiction,” talks about a rite of passage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/28/arts/television/chris-colfer-the-first-time-i-visited-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'The “Glee” actor and best-selling author, whose latest young adult novel is “Stranger Than Fanfiction,” talks about a rite of passage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine, if you will, the Pillsbury Doughboy with Peter Brady’s haircut and Truman Capote’s voice. Add a sprinkling of the fear of being touched and the social anxiety of a shy Chihuahua. That was me at 18, and in December 2008, that guy decided it was a good idea to take a trip to New York City all by himself.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/02/arts/02FIRSTTIME2/02FIRSTTIME2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 806, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/04/02/arts/02FIRSTTIME2/02FIRSTTIME2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 806}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/02/arts/02FIRSTTIME2/02FIRSTTIME2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 763, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/02/arts/02FIRSTTIME2/02FIRSTTIME2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1525, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/02/arts/02FIRSTTIME2/02FIRSTTIME2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/04/02/arts/02FIRSTTIME2/02FIRSTTIME2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/02/arts/02FIRSTTIME2/02FIRSTTIME2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chris Colfer: The First Time I Braved New York (and a Taxi!)', 'kicker': 'The First Time', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '… I Braved New York (and a Taxi!)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Glee (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-28T21:15:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Colfer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Colfer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ecfd8cd-5207-5efa-a423-343666c89db2', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ecfd8cd-5207-5efa-a423-343666c89db2'}, {'abstract': 'The latest from Enrique Olvera opens, Angelica Kitchen closes, and other restaurant news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/28/dining/enrique-olvera-atla-chefs-club-counter.html', 'snippet': 'The latest from Enrique Olvera opens, Angelica Kitchen closes, and other restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHEFS CLUB COUNTER At this extension of Chefs Club, the NoLIta restaurant where chefs from around the globe are invited to cook, Stephane De Baets, the company’s president and founder, is taking a new tack on fast-casual dining featuring a rotating roster of specialties from prominent chefs. “We pay chefs a fee to use their recipes, and they get royalties for sales,” he said. Mr. De Baets was not forthcoming on the financial details because not all the chefs are paid the same amount, though each is guaranteed a minimum. The recipes will be featured for around three months, then other chefs’ dishes will rotate in. The first round will feature breakfast sandwiches from Alvin Cailan of Eggslut in Los Angeles; a ham-and-cheese on baguette from Eric Kayser; a burger from Jean-Georges Vongerichten; and duck rice from George Mendes’s Aldea menu. Linton Hopkins from Atlanta will offer a grain bowl, and there will also be Roman-style pizza by Magnus Hansson. At the spacious restaurant, done in creamy tile with glove-leather upholstery, customers order food at a counter and get a buzzer alert when it’s ready. Beer and wine are served. Mr. De Baets is considering expanding to other locations. (Opens Friday): 62 Spring Street (Lafayette Street), 646-438-9172, chefsclubcounter.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/dining/29OFF/29OFF-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/29/dining/29OFF/29OFF-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/dining/29OFF/29OFF-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/dining/29OFF/29OFF-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1387, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/dining/29OFF/29Off-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/29/dining/29OFF/29Off-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/dining/29OFF/29Off-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rotating Recipes at Chefs Club Counter in NoLIta', 'kicker': 'Off the Menu', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 