e, 'print_headline': 'Ivory Prices May Mean a Reprieve for Elephants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elephants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poaching (Wildlife)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ivory', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Save the Elephants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-29T14:43:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f1dfbee-a051-5431-a255-f69ae31289cd', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f1dfbee-a051-5431-a255-f69ae31289cd'}, {'abstract': 'President Erdogan’s tough talk on Europe and move for unfettered power could mark a fateful retreat from the Westernization that had long guided Turkey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/29/opinion/turkeys-dangerous-path-away-from-democracy.html', 'snippet': 'President Erdogan’s tough talk on Europe and move for unfettered power could mark a fateful retreat from the Westernization that had long guided Turkey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Authoritarian leaders have long appreciated the power of fanning fears of real or perceived enemies to garner popular support. President Recep Tayyip Erdogan of Turkey is good at this. He has exploited a conflict with Kurdish insurgents and a failed coup to win elections and wage a brutal crackdown on critics, and now he is picking a fight with Europe to rally support for a referendum next month on constitutional changes that would essentially give him unfettered power. The tactic might get him some votes, but like the powers he seeks, it has dangerous consequences for Turkey’s future.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/30/world/30editorial-inyt-1/30editorial-inyt-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/30/world/30editorial-inyt-1/30editorial-inyt-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/30/world/30editorial-inyt-1/30editorial-inyt-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/30/world/30editorial-inyt-1/30editorial-inyt-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/30/world/30editorial-inyt-1/30editorial-inyt-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/30/world/30editorial-inyt-1/30editorial-inyt-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/30/world/30editorial-inyt-1/30editorial-inyt-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkey’s Dangerous Path Away From Democracy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turkey’s Path Away From Democracy