n', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Freedom Caucus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanford, Mark', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-30T20:21:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Martin and Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/199c9ab7-9f6f-5bc9-a07b-5553e3e37e28', 'word_count': 1100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/199c9ab7-9f6f-5bc9-a07b-5553e3e37e28'}, {'abstract': 'This documentary captures the antic personality of Mr. Conrad, an avant-garde musician and experimental filmmaker who died last year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/30/movies/tony-conrad-completely-in-the-present-review.html', 'snippet': 'This documentary captures the antic personality of Mr. Conrad, an avant-garde musician and experimental filmmaker who died last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While he conceived and created some of the most prescient, influential and galvanic music of the second half of the 20th century, Tony Conrad would have bristled if you had called him a composer. “One of the things the music represented was the absence of the composer,” Mr. Conrad says in the new documentary “Tony Conrad: Completely in the Present.” He considered this to be the case for his early ’60s work with John Cale, Marian Zazeela, Angus MacLise and, most crucially, La Monte Young — someone who very much considers himself a composer. Mr. Conrad’s ideological break with Mr. Young is one of the many fascinating episodes of Mr. Conrad’s productive life (he died last April at  76) covered in this film directed by Tyler Hubby.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/arts/tony-conrad/tony-conrad-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/31/arts/tony-conrad/tony-conrad-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 342}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/arts/tony-conrad/tony-conrad-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 583, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/arts/tony-conrad/tony-conrad-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1166, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/arts/tony-conrad/tony-conrad-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/31/arts/tony-conrad/tony-conrad-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/arts/tony-conrad/tony-conrad-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Revi