 Linda Bishop, who had a psychotic disorder and fell through the cracks of New Hampshire’s medical establishment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2011, The New Yorker published “God Knows Where I Am,” an unsettling article by Rachel Aviv recounting the fate of Linda Bishop, a single mother with bipolar disorder and psychosis who fell through the cracks of New Hampshire’s medical establishment. Now Ms. Aviv is a consulting producer for Jedd and Todd Wider’s affecting documentary of the same title, which adds vivid colors to the tragic tale.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/arts/31GODKNOWS/31GODKNOWS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/31/arts/31GODKNOWS/31GODKNOWS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 652}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/arts/31GODKNOWS/31GODKNOWS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 947, 'width': 871, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/arts/31GODKNOWS/31GODKNOWS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 947, 'width': 871, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/arts/31GODKNOWS/31GODKNOWS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/31/arts/31GODKNOWS/31GODKNOWS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/arts/31GODKNOWS/31GODKNOWS-thumbL