 long-delayed infusion of funds to some of its lowest-performing schools after it had frozen the money because it said not all of the schools qualified.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/30/nyregion/new-york-state-persistently-failing-schools.html', 'snippet': 'The state budget authority released a long-delayed infusion of funds to some of its lowest-performing schools after it had frozen the money because it said not all of the schools qualified.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A tangled court battle that pitted New York’s budget authority against its Education Department took another turn on Wednesday when the state released a long-delayed infusion of cash to some of its lowest-performing schools.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/nyregion/31funding/31funding-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/31/nyregion/31funding/31funding-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/nyregion/31funding/31funding-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/nyregion/31funding/31funding-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/nyregion/31funding/31funding-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/03/31/nyregion/31funding/31funding-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/nyregion/31funding/31funding-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Money for ‘Failing’ State Schools Has Finally Been Released', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Albany Releases $69 Million for Low-Performing Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-30T22:17:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea9a6f04-9634-5539-87b1-261228c03ba6', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea9a6f04-9634-5539-87b1-261228c03ba6'}, {'abstract': 'Greg Iles’s “Natchez Burning” trilogy amounted to 2,300 pages in three years. The final volume, “Mississippi Blood,” is No. 1 in hardcover fiction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/30/books/review/a-strong-start-for-an-epics-finale.html', 'snippet': 'Greg Iles’s “Natchez Burning” trilogy amounted to 2,300 pages in three years. The final volume, “Mississippi Blood,” is No. 1 in hardcover fiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Secret Realities: The suspense novel “Mississippi Blood,” new at No.\u202f1 on the hardcover fiction list, concludes Greg Iles’s mammoth Natchez Burning trilogy, about race, murder and a fraught father-son relationship spanning half a century in the Deep South. Before the trilogy started with “Natchez Burning” in 2014, Iles had written a number of previous best sellers featuring its protagonist, the lawyer Penn Cage, and early drafts of “Natchez Burning” treated that book as another straightforward thriller along the same lines. But after a serious car accident in 2011 — Iles lost a leg and spent months recuperating — he returned to the book with a new sense of purpose and an ambition reflected in the trilogy’s ultimate size: more than 2,300 pages published over the course of three years. (At that rate, Robert Caro could have wrapped up his Lyndon Johnson biography decades ago and moved on to a multivolume study of Gerald Ford.)', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/09/books/review/09insidelist/09insidelist-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/04/09/books/review/09insidelist/09insidelist-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 613}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/09/books/review/09insidelist/09insidelist-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 855, 'width': 837, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/09/books/review/09insidelist/09insidelist-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 855, 'width': 837, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/09/books/review/09insidelist/09insidelist-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subT