ue': 'Coal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-31T07:21:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Bloomberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Bloomberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/279fd3bb-cb74-5e5f-a2e6-ab0c3f8668a7', 'word_count': 916, 'uri': 'nyt://article/279fd3bb-cb74-5e5f-a2e6-ab0c3f8668a7'}, {'abstract': 'Its members make impossible demands and refuse to compromise. This is not the way to govern.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/31/opinion/how-the-freedom-caucus-is-undermining-the-gop.html', 'snippet': 'Its members make impossible demands and refuse to compromise. This is not the way to govern.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Governing is not easy. We learned this the hard way as Speaker Paul Ryan stood before House Republicans last week and told us he was withdrawing the Obamacare replacement plan. Despite campaign promises to repeal and replace by the president and most Republicans, the votes were not there to pass the American Health Care Act. And just like that, the effort was dead.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/31/opinion/31kinzingerWeb/31kinzingerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/31/opinion/31kinzingerWeb/31kinzingerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewi