, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-31T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/538e4d8e-5404-5179-93a7-6843dfac596a', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/538e4d8e-5404-5179-93a7-6843dfac596a'}, {'abstract': 'Should The Times use “reform” sparingly? And did an obituary play down a man’s experience with discrimination?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/31/public-editor/friday-mailbag-reforming-the-use-of-reform.html', 'snippet': 'Should The Times use “reform” sparingly? And did an obituary play down a man’s experience with discrimination?', 'lead_paragraph': 'With repeal of the Affordable Care Act on the back burner, Republicans have moved forward with plans for a sizable tax cut, and so, too, did The New York Times’s coverage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/opinion/01pubedmailart/01pubedmailart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 454, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/03/29/opinion/01pubedmailart/01pubedmailart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 454}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/opinion/01pubedmailart/01pubedmailart-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/03/29/opinion/01pubedmailart/01pubedmailart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1548, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_na