ype_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9f07bb3-7aa8-50f7-beb3-ef887c22bd21', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9f07bb3-7aa8-50f7-beb3-ef887c22bd21'}, {'abstract': 'The B.D.S. movement uses the comparison as a cynical slogan. But those who lived under apartheid know the difference.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/31/opinion/why-israel-is-nothing-like-apartheid-south-africa.html', 'snippet': 'The B.D.S. movement uses the comparison as a cynical slogan. But those who lived under apartheid know the difference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Among critics of Israel, it has become ever more common to accuse the Jewish state of imitating apartheid South Africa. This month, an obscure United Nations agency, the Economic and Social Commission for Western Asia, whose membership comprises 18 Arab states, caused an uproar when it issued a report accusing Israel of applying the same racism in its conflict with Palestinians that made South Africa an international pariah. The United Nations secretary general swiftly repudiated the report, and it was removed from the agency’s website.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01pogrund-inyt/01pogrund-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01pogrund-inyt/01pogrund-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01pogrund-inyt/01pogrund-inyt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01pogrund-inyt/01pogrund-inyt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01pogrund-inyt/01pogrund-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01pogrund-inyt/01pogrund-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01pogrund-inyt/01pogrund-inyt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Israel Is Nothing Like Apartheid South Africa', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Israel is nothing like apartheid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apartheid (Policy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boycott, Divestment and Sanctions (BDS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-31T11:26:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Pogrund', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrund', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/500368e7-10cf-5635-afa5-2c7e9af46ce0', 'word_count': 1390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/500368e7-10cf-5635-afa5-2c7e9af46ce0'}, {'abstract': 'Someone new to the work force wonders how to deal with a bawdy, oversharing, gossipy co-worker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/31/jobs/workologist-career-advice-irritating-coworker.html', 'snippet': 'Someone new to the work force wonders how to deal with a bawdy, oversharing, gossipy co-worker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I share an office with another woman, whom I can’t stand. She comes in late and complains about how tired she is, overshares her personal relationship issues and tells sexual jokes that make me uncomfortable. Worst of all, she gossips about other people in the office, which I find terribly unprofessional. Some of these issues extend to a chatty culture among others who work on this floor.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/01/22/business/22workologist1/21workologist-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/01/22/business/22workologist1/21workologist-illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/01/22/business/22workologist1/21workologist-illo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/01/22/business/22workologist1/21workologist-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/01/22/business/22workologist1/21workologist-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/01/22/business/22workologist1/21workologist-illo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/01/22/business/22workologist1/21workologist-illo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1091, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Headphones Won’t Solve the Problem of a Chatty Colleague', 'kicker': 'The Workologist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fending Off Obnoxious Chatter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shoket, Ann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Big Life (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-31T11:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Walker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cf1c170-9acf-5498-ab0b-bd9cb1edd3ba', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cf1c170-9acf-5498-ab0b-bd9cb1edd3ba'}, {'abstract': 'A commission’s recommendation to close Rikers Island, and move prisoners to smaller jails in New York City, has won the support of Mayor Bill de Blasio.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/31/nyregion/mayor-de-blasio-is-said-to-back-plan-to-close-jails-on-rikers-island.html', 'snippet': 'A commission’s recommendation to close Rikers Island, and move prisoners to smaller jails in New York City, has won the support of Mayor Bill de Blasio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio vowed on Friday to close the troubled jail complex on Rikers Island, which has spawned federal investigations, brought waves of protests and became a byword for brutality, in a move he said was intended to end an era of mass incarceration in New York City.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/nyregion/01rikers/01rikers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/04/01/nyregion/01rikers/01rikers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/nyregion/01rikers/01rikers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/nyregion/01rikers/01rikers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/nyregion/01rikers/01rikers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/04/01/nyregion/01rikers/01rikers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/nyregion/01rikers/01rikers-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayor Backs Plan to Close Rikers and Open Jails Elsewhere', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'De Blasio Vows to Close Rikers, Ending an Era', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rikers Island Prison Complex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Correction Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lippman, Jonathan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mark-Viverito, Melissa', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-31T11:37:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4844065b-4fe3-5951-957f-cf76e485d2a0', 'word_count': 1307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4844065b-4fe3-5951-957f-cf76e485d2a0'}, {'abstract': 'South Korea’s ousted president was detained before dawn on corruption charges, and the comedown in her circumstances could not have been more stark.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/31/world/asia/park-geun-hye-arrest-jail-south-korea.html', 'snippet': 'South Korea’s ousted president was detained before dawn on corruption charges, and the comedown in her circumstances could not have been more stark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — As president of South Korea, Park Geun-hye never appeared in public until stylists had arranged her hair in the trademark updo of her mother, a popular