hurt when a bridge section collapsed on I-85 on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — Schools were closed, businesses were encouraging employees to work from home, and traffic was extensively rerouted on Friday, a day after a section of Interstate 85, one of the main highways in the Atlanta area, collapsed from a fire.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/us/01collapse2_xp/01collapse2_xp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/04/01/us/01collapse2_xp/01collapse2_xp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/us/01collapse2_xp/01collapse2_xp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/us/01collapse2_xp/01collapse2_xp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/us/01collapse2_xp/01collapse2_xp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/04/01/us/01collapse2_xp/01collapse2_xp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/us/01collapse2_xp/01collapse2_xp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Atlanta Interstate Collapse Sends City’s Commute into Chaos', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deal, Nathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coca-Cola Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-31T14:47:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Fausset and Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fausset', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fe76e0f-c0f8-5e74-9143-c2020916d89f', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fe76e0f-c0f8-5e74-9143-c2020916d89f'}, {'abstract': 'The duo behind the weekly podcast “Another Round” spend Sundays together as often as they can, shopping, grabbing brunch and people watching.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/31/nyregion/heben-nigatu-tracy-clayton-another-round.html', 'snippet': 'The duo behind the weekly podcast “Another Round” spend Sundays together as often as they can, shopping, grabbing brunch and people watching.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heben Nigatu and Tracy Clayton, hosts of the BuzzFeed podcast “Another Round,” seem to have a knack for getting their guests, which have included Hillary Clinton and Lin Manuel Miranda, to open up. They have discussed race relations and anger issues with the comedian Margaret Cho and rom-com favorites with the writer Ta-Nehisi Coates (his is “The 40-Year-Old Virgin”). Booze is a constant in-studio companion — at the end of each episode, Ms. Nigatu and Ms. Clayton each “buy a round” for something they appreciate. On April 7, they will put on a live show at the Bell House, in Brooklyn, as part of the New York City Podcast Festival. Ms. Nigatu, 26, lives in Crown Heights, Brooklyn. Ms. Clayton, 34, lives in Flatbush, Brooklyn. They spend Sundays together as often as they can, shopping and people watching. TAMMY La GORCE', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/02/nyregion/02ROUTINE3sub/02ROUTINE3sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/04/02/nyregion/02ROUTINE3sub/02ROUTINE3sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/02/nyregion/02ROUTINE3sub/02ROUTINE3sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/02/nyregion/02ROUTINE3sub/02ROUTINE3sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/02/nyregion/02ROUTINE3sub/02ROUTINE3sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/04/02/nyregion/02ROUTINE3sub/02ROUTINE3sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/02/nyregion/02ROUTINE3sub/02ROUTINE3sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge'