ract': 'Global soccer’s governing body said on Friday that it had concluded a 22-month inquiry that drew on witness interviews and millions of documents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/31/sports/soccer/fifa-investigation-scandal.html', 'snippet': 'Global soccer’s governing body said on Friday that it had concluded a 22-month inquiry that drew on witness interviews and millions of documents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly two years after a sweeping corruption case first felled top leaders of FIFA, the Swiss-based governing body for international soccer announced on Friday that it had cataloged its officials’ wrongdoing and delivered the results of a 22-month internal investigation to government authorities.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/sports/01FIFA-WEB/01FIFA-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 325, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/04/01/sports/01FIFA-WEB/01FIFA-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 325}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/sports/01FIFA-WEB/01FIFA-WEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 554, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/sports/01FIFA-WEB/01FIFA-WEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1109, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/sports/01FIFA-WEB/01FIFA-WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/04/01/sports/01FIFA-WEB/01FIFA-WEB-thumbSta