/87fd6d77-6ad6-5367-87ce-4d1a06e18a02'}, {'abstract': 'The federal appeals panel held that disclosing the videotapes would create national security risks, and that this concern superseded any public right to see the tapes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/31/us/politics/guantanamo-detainees-force-feeding-videos.html', 'snippet': 'The federal appeals panel held that disclosing the videotapes would create national security risks, and that this concern superseded any public right to see the tapes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The military is allowed to keep secret at least 28 videotapes showing guards at the Guantánamo Bay wartime prison extracting a hunger-striking detainee from his cell and then force-feeding him, a federal appeals court ruled on Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/us/01GITMO-01/01GITMO-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/04/01/us/01GITMO-01/01GITMO-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/us/01GITMO-01/01GITMO-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/us/01GITMO-01/01GITMO-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/us/01GITMO-01/01GITMO-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/04/01/us/01GITMO-01/01GITMO-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/us/01GITMO-01/01GITMO-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Videos of Force-Feeding at Guantánamo Will Stay Secret, Court Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Upholds Secrecy of Guantánamo Videos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunger Strikes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-31T23:48:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2709700c-5e2e-572b-8dcf-2ddbfefeb2fa', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2709700c-5e2e-572b-8dcf-2ddbfefeb2fa'}, {'abstract': 'Will he be able to win over Democrats? What if he needs the support of the Freedom Caucus?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/31/opinion/trump-the-centrist-president.html', 'snippet': 'Will he be able to win over Democrats? What if he needs the support of the Freedom Caucus?', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — When President Trump retreats from a fight, he tends to do so with guns blazing. After a few days of hinting that he might be willing to work with congressional Democrats, this week he unloaded on the Republican Freedom Caucus with both barrels. Mr. Trump learned long ago to never admit a mistake, so  his Twitter attack on Thursday placing the blame for the failure of health care legislation on those conservative Republicans was designed to clear the path for him to reach across party lines.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01schnurWeb/01schnurWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01schnurWeb/01schnurWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01schnurWeb/01schnurWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01schnurWeb/01schnurWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1314, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01schnurWeb/01schnurWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01schnurWeb/01schnurWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01schnurWeb/01schnurWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump, the Centrist President', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Freedom Caucus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2017-03-31T23:51:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Schnur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schnur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0238100-535d-5e54-a6b4-87b800f3d129', 'word_count': 761, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0238100-535d-5e54-a6b4-87b800f3d129'}, {'abstract': 'Flying high above a combat zone helped me understand what was happening on the ground.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2017/03/31/opinion/in-the-air-over-vietnam.html', 'snippet': 'Flying high above a combat zone helped me understand what was happening on the ground.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The heat was suffocating as we got off the Continental charter flight that late summer afternoon in 1966 at South Vietnam’s sprawling Bien Hoa Air Base, but I was more amazed at the incredible activity everywhere. There were other charter planes arriving, constant flights of F-100 and F-5 fighters taking off and landing, lumbering C-130 transports loading and unloading. There was a U-2 circling above the base as it soared to high altitudes for a reconnaissance mission. There were lines of soldiers getting onto another Continental flight, heading home. I soon learned that the thing everyone in the military kept track of, even more than the daily body count, was the countdown to rotating home — “121 days and counting,” someone would say. I was scheduled to rotate home in late 1967.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01schell1web/01schell1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 888, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01schell1web/01schell1web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 888}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01schell1web/01schell1web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 693, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01schell1web/01schell1web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1296, 'width': 876, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01schell1web/01schell1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01schell1web/01schell1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/04/01/opinion/01schell1web/01schell1web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Air Over Vietnam', 'kicker': "Vietnam '67",